d a field the schema does not have.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1703:- **PRD §12** now holds c8's system prompt, closing check and schema, byte for byte the frozen files. Its introduction records the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1707:- **Tests.** The fixtures were brought to the adopted schema: `figures`, plus the four opening fields of a new thesis. Two tests now\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1872:- Preflight: 395 stored answers judged under the c9 schema, 0 refusals.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2328:  - Frozen: the c8 request, schema, model settings and retry (D380, D387), and the committed Step 2 and Step 3 code.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2814:**Design v3:** `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md`, with the drafts `ladder/candidate-system.txt` and `candidate-schema.json`.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2874:   company's quarterly figure and except an obligation from the year limit; the schema's `no_ladder` description and the closing\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2883:Version 7 answers these: the request, schema and checks state the same four refusal cases and the same object rule (another\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2890:2. a pending regulatory decision with no date fitted neither due-day basis; the request named no unit list while the schema closed it;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2892:4. the control arm had no request or schema to audit; the direction mark was applied to yes/no ladders, which have no direction;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2898:control's request is built by code from v74i's lines 20–26 and 35 (`ladder/control-system.txt`, `control-schema.json`); marks apply\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2925:2. **\"The request, the schema and the checks disagree.\"** One table holds every case where no question is written, with what each of\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3062:- **Second blind audit** (`gy-audit-codex.md`), on the changed request and schema without the worked examples: every sentence and\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3159:3. an answer that is not JSON or does not fit the schema raises before the checks and had no outcome;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3165:transport, not reread from the archive; a malformed or schema-invalid answer is a refusal like any other.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3175:- **Numbers.** One set, the same in the request, the schema's descriptions and the check: zero, or a size from 1e-9 to 1e18 with at\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3188:   production's `model.check_schema`, which tests a list's minimum only. Twenty reviews and I had read \"the schema says five\" as\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3189:   \"five is enforced\". Check 1 now counts; the schema drops both length keywords, since no stored request has sent `maxItems` to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3356:- *What is sent:* the request of design version 30 (system text; the payload, a blank line, the closing check; the strict schema;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3371:the schema; five ladders and one refusal; $0.0059. Read by me beside the articles (`READING-claude.md`, written first) and by a\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3462:   so the wrong label cannot be written (AGENTS §3: a contract a schema can enforce is enforced there).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3468:**The shape change** (`ladder/candidate-schema.json`, `candidate-system.txt`, `candidate-closing.txt`; the third send's request is\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3477:- **Council before the send** (`council/iq-codex.md`): hold for a stale description in the schema and for the theme's name field\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3522:  more calls. `first-schema-as-sent.json` is the first schema rebuilt in that order and equal to the archived one, order aside.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3526:and the request agrees with its schema. System text 7,123 to 7,627 characters; closing as first sent.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3536:- **By D407:** the request is the first request (`ladder/candidate-*` restored to it, the schema in the order sent; the arms are\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3718:| three outcomes | the gaps and overlaps of event answers come from the division beyond three outcomes and from a Yes whose No is not its complement; if code writes every rung but the two conditions, exactly one rung holds by construction | the schema's `yes_no` and `states` become `event` (`happened`, `ruled_out` or null); one paragraph of the system text and one sentence of the closing check; code writes `Happened`, `Ruled out` (\"holds only when rung 1 does not\") and `Neither` or `Not happened`; the five-state check and its tests retired | eight theses of the first run that had a gap or an overlap, answered by hand: all pass the schema, the checks and the view writer, and every former gap lands in one rung (`stage_a/result/three-outcomes-by-hand.txt`); 111 tests; mutants 41, 11 and 16 caught; the first run's report reproduced unchanged by the new accounting code | not yet: council `iw` (Codex) and `ix` (a Claude reader on the by-hand answers) first |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:3753:  caught; eight by-hand answers pass the schema and the checks. Round three (`iz`) is with the reviewer. Nothing has been sent.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4043:| the reference | the mark both readers fail most on figures (10 ladders in the second run) comes from a field that cannot hold what the article says: a reported amount has only \"expected\" to go under, and a range has no place | `reference` gains `kind` (expected, last_reported) and `value_to`; check 6 places a range by its middle and refuses a reported amount on an event; the judge's middle rung says \"the amount last reported\"; the request's paragraph and the closing check's sentence rewritten (system text 6,872 to 7,276 characters, closing check 812 to 966: growth, for two kinds and a range where there was one kind and one number) | the second run's own answers for two reported-amount theses, the range thesis and a control, with only the reference rewritten by hand: all pass the schema and the checks; the judge's text reads \"the amount last reported\" for the $119 billion and carries the 50 to 60 percent passage where it said \"no reference figure\" (`stage_a/result-2/reference-by-hand.txt`); 118 tests; mutants 47, 11 and 16 caught | not yet: council `je` first |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4060:  paragraph, the schema and the closing check said the same thing three times (trimmed). A reference in words alone is not\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4191:  run follow the old arm's schema in the order of their keys at every level, and a reversed schema is told apart. The arms\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4424:| D416, the typed ruling out | a free sentence lets the wait be written as the ruling out; a typed answer (who decides, what they decide) leaves it no place | the event paragraph, the closing check's event sentence, the schema; code reads either shape (`ruling_out_of`) and gives the same three rungs | on the stored sentences: no place for six of the seven faults, a place for the 121 sound ones, the seventh not excluded; a hand-written typed answer passes its schema, the checks and the view writer; 130 tests, 58 of 58 mutants | not yet: council `jt` first |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4433:**Councils `jt` (do not send: the survey arm's schema still listed six cases; a missing readable control must be \"not proved\")\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4518:  checks (the event one against the schema of its time); the third run's 108 stored ladders through the checks as they\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4519:  stand (none refused); the typed arm's 30 stored answers through the working schema and checks (30 fit, 30 accepted).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4793:- Found by my own dry run: a schema misfit was treated as a stop that a second send cannot change; it now gets the redo.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4931:- *D433 (Alex: \"开 c14，先小测\").* Before the first send: production sends an adapted request (the schema in the system text, JSON-\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:4966:  schema. Final sizes against c8: c15yc +332 characters, c15c +91.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-system.txt:102:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-system.txt:172:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/lfile-system.txt:161:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/ACCEPTANCE-PROTOCOL.md:9:- `arms/c8-system.txt`, `arms/c8-closing.txt` and `arms/c8-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/focused/focused_probe.py:20:SCHEMA = json.loads((HERE / 'schema.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/focused/focused_probe.py:136:        schema_errors = model.check_schema(data, SCHEMA)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/focused/focused_probe.py:137:        record['contract_errors'] = schema_errors[:5] if schema_errors else check(data, routed_ids, thesis_ids)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/k6b-system.txt:159:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/probe6_diagnose.py:12:d