mpty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c9-system.txt:106:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c9-system.txt:180:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c5-system.txt:166:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-12.md:13:   The draft has **one example per case**. AGENTS §6 asks for **two or three per class**. Use varied industries, and avoid reproducing the test article’s combined-spending scenario merely with names removed. Audit every example against the standard, the schema and the closing check. [Standard §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:344)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c13-schema.json:54:       \"shared_quantity\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c16-schema.json:54:       \"shared_quantity\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c13-system.txt:102:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c13-system.txt:172:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cr-handoff.md:4:- the system text `system.txt`, with the schema `schema.json` appended after \"Return only one JSON object that conforms to this JSON\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c12-system.txt:103:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c12-system.txt:173:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c3-system.txt:169:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:102:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:172:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ht-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ht-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mm-challenge-2.md:20:matter), and which correct theses they could break (D441's warning). Strongest argument against: a schema change is a large new Step 1\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1k-system.txt:163:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ae-claude.md:4:1. **c4 prompt** (Alex's D209 second amendment): the role and schema say unlinked items are kept; the closing read-back says a ruled-out\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u1ku3-system.txt:163:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u3-system.txt:159:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hh-codex.md:13:The remaining review work is material: walk all eight fixtures through every check and written row; audit every request and schema sentence against its cited source; check the three design tables against their actual readers and old checks; and trace the claims from `dryrun3` through `dryrun8` and `reference` to the saved answers. Until those are done, I cannot answer whether a wrong answer escapes all reader marks, whether two engineers could implement different behavior, or whether all six Stage A lines can fail and cannot pass for a wrong reason.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ik-audit-handoff.md:12:- the answer schema with every description: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ik-audit-handoff.md:30:  stated above it; an example must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer; the request never asks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ik-audit-handoff.md:36:1. **Request to standard.** A table with one row per sentence of the system text (number them), per schema description, and per\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cl-handoff.md:18:- the arms `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/{c8,c10a,c10b,c11}-{system.txt,closing.txt,schema.json}`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/if-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/if-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/kf-codex.md:39:There is a presentation limitation: production attaches replacement and revision context to evidence records, while `not_shown_of` returns only selected fields and does not attach that context. The membership test may be right while a reader lacks context needed to assess E in a case with replacements or revisions. The code also calls the user-message text `request_as_sent`; it does **not** include the actual system message or schema. The form supplies the judge’s rules separately, but the label overstates what is in each packet. [Stored judgements](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/stored_judgements.py:27)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/be-codex.md:11:- “**material … return it with empty links**”; “**never open … only to give a statement a home**,” repeated in the closing check and `links` schema — **consistent** with D383 and §4’s separate-opening test.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/be-codex.md:14:- “**answer could change a position**,” publicly settled on a date, and not already asked; “**one quantity for one period, or one event**” — **consistent** with §4’s three requirements and writing rule. The schema’s `period`, `settled_by`, closest question and separate-bet descriptions carry these requirements.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/be-codex.md:15:- The four reasons — “**product_node**,” “**binding_obligation**,” “**shared_quantity**,” “**policy_stage**” — and “**fits none … never a thesis**” — **consistent** with D384, which removes the standard’s main financial-quantity class under D382. Their dates and examples generally follow §3.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15c-schema.json:54:       \"shared_quantity\",\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iz-codex.md:24:5. **请求全文。** 事件的发生、否决和可否为 null 在正文、schema 和末尾复核中各出现一次；这是三处重复，末尾用于复核。三处现在没有“every way”与“plain ways”的冲突。仍有一处实质张力：正文先说条件不得重叠，合并示例却允许先批准、后阻止都满足各自文字；代码靠第一档优先消除最终重叠，但模型看不到这条优先规则。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hm-audit-codex.md:3:以下是独立判断；完成后才读取作者表和前三次审计。`S` 是[系统文本](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt)的“行号.该行内句序”；`J` 是[schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json)的描述行号；`P` 是[冻结提示词](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13)。表中的“一致”包括为执行已决定规则而规定的输出格式。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hm-audit-codex.md:79:| J235 `reference.words` | D260、D398 | **更窄**：[J235](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:235)对数字题排除纯文字预期，同 S16.2。 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hm-audit-codex.md:100:并购例子逐项走查：批准时“有条件／无条件”互斥且覆盖两种；未决定时“撤回／未撤回”互斥且覆盖两种；否决是第五种。按例子采用的**批准／未决定／否决**三类结果，五者不重叠，也没有遗漏；到期日当天的结果落入当天状态。例子没有完整回答，因此不能单独验证对象、日期和其他 schema 检查。[S13](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt:13)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jt-codex.md:1:1. **The survey arm contradicts itself.** [survey-system.txt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/probe-d416-d418-2026-11-10/survey-system.txt:6) adds a seventh reason to decline; [survey-schema.json](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/probe-d416-d418-2026-11-10/survey-schema.json:19) still lists only the original six. The model reads both. Also, a non-year period *with* a stated publication day is not declined by the new sentence, but the figure schema can express only a year; that pre-existing boundary remains unresolved.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jt-codex.md:3:   The typed arm’s instruction is consistent across its paragraph, schema and closing check. The code checks that both strings are nonempty; it does not check that the named party made the decision or that the decision rules out the event. “The authority decided to continue investigating” can still fit. The merger example is general, not taken from a test article.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jt-codex.md:11:**Do not send:** first make the survey schema agree with its seventh reason, and make missing readable controls an unproved result.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-system.txt:102:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for one calendar year, this year or next (a\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c17-system.txt:174:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/b-claude.md:23:- **u3**: the required per-item decision in the schema (+560 characters).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bn-codex.md:1:**Both arms are NOT READY.** The final read-back now clearly preserves a qualifying unsigned obligation beside an open total, but both schemas still require the model to explain “how their answers can move apart.”\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/z-codex.md:7:A wording note: the system says to list **useful** figures, while the [schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c2-schema.json:189) says a statement with several figures “lists them all.” Align those descriptions.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hc-codex.md:5:2. **The number check sees a parsed number, not necessarily the number written.** [DESIGN.md:292](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:292) promises to preserve the answer’s number, but [model.py:260](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:260) parses JSON with `json.loads` first. For example, `9007199254740993.0` has already rounded before the proposed comparison; it can pass as `9007199254740992.0`. The claim that every number with at most fifteen significant digits is representable is also false for `1e400`, which the request permits but the check refuses. Specify parsing, permitted magnitude and precision, and refusal consistently across request, schema and check. Test decimal-form integers and exponent overflow as well as integer literals.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hc-codex.md:15:**Contract and request.** I found no written-label or interval discrepancy in the eight fixtures. Their use as check fixtures is compatible with separate planted semantic tests; they do not establish that their answers are sound. I did not establish an answer that passes every check and cannot be caught by any reader mark. The closing check repeats earlier requirements, and the request’s examples are not fitted to the covered company. The overflow example above is a request/check conflict. I have **not completed an independent sentence-by-sentence audit of every schema description and original source**, so that remains an open verification.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15c-system.txt:102:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15c-system.txt:172:Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jz-challenge.md:13:shape into the working request, its closing check and its schema; bring the readers' form to D418 (mark O), D420 (mark R)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lc-handoff.md:6:its owner … the schema beside the field\", §7.3 one class at a time). Alex chose (D432 in `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`) a diagnosis of\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hj-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hj-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hj-handoff.md:33:## Your angle: the contract (design §5.3 and §5.4; `ladder/examples.json`; `ladder/candidate-schema.json`; `ladder/number_rule_check.py`)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hj-handoff.md:38:1. Walk **each of the eight fixtures** of `examples.json` through the schema (with production's validator, `model.check_schema`\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iu-handoff.md:14:`candidate-schema.json`; the design is `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md`, §5 for the step and §8 from \"Stage A\" for the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iu-handoff.md:46:   for each, where the decision is made (the request's sentence, the schema's field, a code check, the thesis upstream).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bv-challenge.md:1:Design review of arm c11 (read-only). Read `council/bu-claude.md`, then `arms/c11-closing.txt` (last paragraph) and `arms/c11-schema.json` (`company_impact`), against your bt-codex.md limits, D388 and D248 boundary 6. Under 250 words: does the design answer the mechanism, does the field or the read-back conflict with anything in c8, are the falsifiers enough? End with SEND, SEND WITH CHANGES, or DO NOT SEND.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hg-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hg-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hg-handoff.md:36:2. **The contract.** Walk every fixture of `examples.json` through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number rules. Say\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mm-codex-3.md:21:D414 demonstrates a narrower success: once the relevant annual period is already identified, code can calculate a consistent date. It does not establish that code can choose the period, identify the same obligation, or decide whether a comparison deserves its own question. c11 is also a warning rather than a verdict against every schema: its required field was accompanied by other wording, stored answers lacked the field, and its small probe had regressions. [c11 record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2020)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mm-codex-3.md:23:**Stop the typed-unit line** if the audit needs invented field values to demonstrate a catch, mainly produces refusals without a path to recover the question, or cannot distinguish correct comparisons and related evidence from invalid combinations. A $0 audit can establish feasibility and risk; it cannot establish how a model would fill a new schema or the effect on final judgments.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ah-claude.md:3:Scope: `arms/c8-system.txt`, `c8-closing.txt`, `c8-schema.json`. References: the signed standard (§§2–5), D380–D386, Alex's rulings.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ah-claude.md:28:- **Growth:** system 13,476 (K6b) → 15,068 characters; closing 7,670 → 8,534; schema +about 2,400. Reason: Alex's four decisions,\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ft-challenge.md:12:5. **The whole-request audit** used a blind second reader on c12's system text, closing check and schema. Its main finding: the first\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gy-audit-handoff.md:10:- the answer schema with every description: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gy-audit-handoff.md:24:  stated above it; an example must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer; the request never asks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gy-audit-handoff.md:29:1. **Request to standard.** A table with one row per sentence of the system text (number them), per schema description, and per\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gv-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json` and worked examples `examples.json`, as a\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gv-handoff.md:23:3. **The contract (§5, the schema, the examples).** Walk the examples through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lj-codex.md:3:For example, the stored production request puts the output schema in the system message and uses `reasoning_effort: high`. The probe reads the earlier, unadapted request instead, so its c8 comparison would use a different request from the one whose behaviour is being compared.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lj-codex.md:5:1. **The prompt edits are correct; the replay is not.** The system and closing files differ from c8 in exactly the two sentences named in [D433](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4817), and the schema files are byte-identical.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lj-codex.md:7:   The probe reads `trace.request` and sends it directly ([probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/probe_c14.py:32), [send](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/probe_c14.py:81)). Production adapts that request before sending: it appends the schema to the system message, switches to JSON-object mode, and adds reasoning effort ([live transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/live.py:12)). I checked all three main-case traces: each stored `raw_response.sent_request` differs from `trace.request` in those respects, and each has `reasoning_effort: high`. Production records the adapted request specifically for this reason ([runner](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/runner.py:294)).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lj-codex.md:9:   The c8 arm must use the stored **sent** request. The c14 arm must preserve that request, including the appended schema and settings, and replace only the two approved passages. Check the serialized requests against the stored sent requests before any call.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lj-codex.md:15:   The other quoted audit verdicts are reasonable as readings of their individual lines. They do not establish a full request audit: the document explicitly examines the changed and interacting sentences, while the required audit includes the whole request, including schema descriptions ([audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/PROMPT-AUDIT-c14.md:3), [audit procedure](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md:23)). I cannot give an unqualified “every verdict checked” conclusion from this audit.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lk-codex.md:7:   - **Production request: substantially closed.** The probe rebuilds c8 with production’s adapter and refuses a mismatch with the stored `sent_request`; it then replaces the two c14 passages ([probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/probe_c14.py:38)). The two prompt diffs match D433, and the schema files are identical. The separate required comparison of an answer’s key order with a production answer is not shown ([rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:172)).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lk-codex.md:10:   - **Answer retention and failure handling: partly closed.** Successful provider responses and their outcomes are retained, and refusal, finish reason and unlinked questions are handled ([probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/probe_c14.py:103)). But the probe retries *all* `runner.ContractError` failures ([probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/probe_c14.py:121)); production retries schema or format failures before running the additional validation, but does not retry a subsequent contract failure ([runner](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/runner.py:317)). Also, responses are written only after all jobs finish, so an unexpected exception can prevent completed answers from being saved ([probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/probe_c14.py:133)).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ln-handoff.md:6:`c14-closing.txt` (the closing check appended after the item), `c14-schema.json` (the answer schema; production states it at the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ln-handoff.md:12:Task (the prompt-audit procedure, both directions): read the whole c14 request (system, closing, schema descriptions) against the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/je-challenge.md:14:  against\"; `ladder/candidate-closing.txt`, the sentence on the reference; `ladder/candidate-schema.json`, `reference` with\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/je-challenge.md:26:   check and the schema's descriptions; any sentence about the reference with no source in D411 or the paragraph it replaces;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/je-challenge.md:29:2. **What it lets through, and what it will do to answers.** Give a reference that passes the schema and every check and is\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hy-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hy-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hb-codex.md:7:3. **The numeric contract can change the number it receives.** [DESIGN.md:290](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:290) accepts every finite number but stores it as a Python float. For example, `9007199254740993` becomes `9007199254740992.0`; very large finite JSON numbers can overflow float conversion. The promised text-to-*stored-float* round trip does not preserve the number the model supplied. Two engineers could also handle overflow differently. Define conversion, precision and refusal behavior consistently in the request, schema and checks; test both exactly representable and non-representable values. This is still part of **ha finding 3**, despite removing the earlier 2^53 cutoff.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hb-codex.md:15:**Contract and request.** I found no mismatch between the eight fixtures’ written labels, order or interval text and the stated rendering rules. Treating them as code fixtures is reasonable, provided the separate planted semantic tests remain in place. The flawed theme fixture passes the structural checks, but reader marks Q, R and W can catch its defects; I did not establish a wrong answer outside every reader mark. The closing check repeats preceding requirements, and the three request examples are not fitted to the covered company. The source table identifies the event-date rule as deliberately narrower. I have **not completed an independent sentence-by-sentence audit of every schema description against its original source**, so that audit remains an open verification, not a pass.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gm-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt` and `candidate-schema.json`. Read `AGENTS.md` first (§1, §2, §6 and §7\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gm-handoff.md:9:- The design is not READY as a whole: its core contract waits for Alex's answers to C1 and C2 (§4). The request and the schema are\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gm-handoff.md:28:5. **Checks (§5.3) and the schema.** Is each check sourced as cited? Do the schema's two shapes, the checks and the label rule fit\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gm-handoff.md:30:   figure)? Give a concrete answer that passes the schema and the checks and is still a wrong ladder.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lu-handoff.md:18:   - Harness: clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/probe_c14.py (now takes each arm's schema file; production's adapter; a byte check\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gu-codex.md:7:3. **The control’s checks cannot be implemented as written.** The control has `rungs`, `kind` and `year`; it has no `figure`, `states`, `opens_as` or `outcome` in its answer. Yet the design applies check 5’s shape-dependent date and year tests to it without saying how its shape is identified, whether `opens_as` and `outcome` come from the input, or how its stated `kind` is reconciled with the resolved object. Two engineers could reject different answers. [Control schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/control-schema.json:29), [design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:485). Specify the control’s complete validation and mapping, including shuffled ranges, before comparing it.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gu-codex.md:17:**Five answer paths.** Assuming the schema and checks 1–8 pass, each creates a view and ladder record at the opening article’s day and sequence:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gu-codex.md:27:**Request audit.** Against the sources cited in §5.2: lines **1, 4–5, 9, 12, 15–17 and 20–23** are consistent with the stated source or settled decision. Line **6** follows the listed exclusions, subject to the refusal-comparison defect above. Line **13** is narrower for an event with three or four natural states: it demands five. Line **14** is wider than production’s unit list through `other`. Line **25** repeats rules above it; sampling three outcomes does not prove complete coverage. The examples do not visibly fit NVIDIA or a test article. The request allows another company or unlisted theme; check 2 intentionally ends without a view. The promised blind whole-request audit, including schema descriptions, remains outstanding. [Request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt:1).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bk-claude.md:25:- **c10a: the read-back only.** The closing grows from 8,638 to 9,165 characters (+527). System and schema are unchanged.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bk-claude.md:28:  otherwise null.\" The read-back reads \"each statement whose unsigned_obligation is set …\". The closing grows by 389 and the schema\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/al-challenge.md:4:2. Preflight ($0): every stored c7 dev answer replayed through the current `runner.validate` under the c8 schema: 115 judged, 0 schema or contract refusals.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/al-challenge.md:10:8. Prompt growth: system 13,476 → 15,828 (+2,352), closing 7,670 → 8,638 (+968), schema 5,336 → 7,646 (+2,310) characters; prompt tokens on d1-57 9,398 → 10,552 (+1,154, +12%). Each addition carries D382–D385 or an audit amendment (`council/ah-codex.md`, `ai-codex.md`, `aj-codex.md`: READY TO FREEZE).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hb-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hb-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hb-handoff.md:34:2. **The contract.** Walk every fixture of `examples.json` through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number rules. Say\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hd-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hd-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hd-handoff.md:34:2. **The contract.** Walk every fixture of `examples.json` through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number rules. Say\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lt-codex.md:3:There is a naming ambiguity in the hand-off. It asks for the whole **c14** request but identifies **c15** as the candidate and asks for the c8-to-c15 diff. I audited c15 as the candidate and compared both pairs. Against c8, c15 changes four system sentences, one closing sentence, and one schema description. Against c14, it changes two system sentences and the schema description; the shared-quantity year sentence and closing sentence are already in c14.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lt-codex.md:9:| One quantity for one period, or one event ([system, line 89](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15-system.txt:89>); [schema, line 36](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15-schema.json:36>)) | **Consistent** | This carries the standard’s basic unit; separate parts must also be independently worth tracking. [Standard, line 302](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:302>) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lt-codex.md:18:| The schema permits an event’s later date or abandonment as part of its outcome ([schema, line 36](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15-schema.json:36>)) | **Consistent in principle, but ambiguous** | A later date can describe the same event, but this wording does not tell the model the standard’s specific rule for an already-open earlier deadline. It should not be read as permission to open a second deadline question. [Standard, line 348](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:348>) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lt-codex.md:29:| The schema says a separately bettable second quantity or event is its own question when big, otherwise evidence ([schema, line 36](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c15-schema.json:36>)) | **Keeps wider** | Size and a separate bet are not sufficient by themselves: the question must also fit an allowed reason, have public resolution, and pass the other opening tests. The system and closing check state some of these conditions, so the schema’s standalone wording is incomplete. [Standard, lines 297 and 308–318](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:297>) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-13.md:10:   - The candidate gives **two** examples for the “another thesis” class across two different boundaries—another year and an unsigned deal—not two examples for each boundary. Check the examples and categories against AGENTS §6, the whole request and schema. The text also still assigns comparison with the open library to Step 1, a departure from the standard’s allocation that the design discloses but does not resolve.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hw-audit-handoff.md:12:- the answer schema with every description: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hw-audit-handoff.md:28:  stated above it; an example must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer; the request never asks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hw-audit-handoff.md:34:1. **Request to standard.** A table with one row per sentence of the system text (number them), per schema description, and per\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gt-codex.md:13:**The five answer paths.** Assuming the schema and applicable checks pass, all write a view and ladder record with the opening article’s day and sequence:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gt-codex.md:23:**Request audit.** Sentence by sentence against the sources listed in §5.2: lines **1, 4–5, 9, 12, 15–17 and 20–23** are consistent with the cited sources, with line 23 now scoped to `binding_obligation`; line **6** follows the cited restrictions but has the refusal-disposition mismatch above; line **13** is narrower for an event with three or four natural states,