/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hq-audit-codex.md:3:以下 `S` 是[系统文本](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt)的行号及行内句序；`J` 是 [schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json)的描述行号；`P` 是[冻结生产文本](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13)。同一行内的句子分别编号。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hq-audit-codex.md:49:| J263 `due_day_basis` | P16、26 | **更窄**：同 S22。[J263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:263) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/aj-challenge.md:1:Re-check after edits (read-only). c8 files edited per your amendments: the cash example is an illustration with \"usually\" in §2 and in the closing read-back (\"for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes\"); \"unfiled\" removed everywhere (role, §2 label \"NO THESIS YET\", closing); linking \"to every thesis it informs …; use the narrowest relevant thesis only when choosing between theses that cover the same thing\"; opening test \"its answer could change a position because it could change the company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk, or competitive position in a way you can name; … A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event.\"; dates by reason (undertaken obligation → next annual report; unsigned → check date within 18 months; pending regulation → fiscal year-end; shared quantity and product event only when the item supports a date; otherwise rewritten or not opened) and the schema's period description aligned; the two added examples carry their context; the valuation wording made unconditional in the closing.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/z-challenge.md:2:- \"lists its useful figures in figures\" (aligned with the schema's \"useful\");\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/z-challenge.md:5:- Growth (indent-1 counts): system +975, closing +138, schema +1,717 (field definitions beside the fields). Nothing was cut because c2 restores K6b text c1 had removed and the remaining additions are the new contract.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/id-audit-handoff.md:12:- the answer schema with every description: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/id-audit-handoff.md:28:  stated above it; an example must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer; the request never asks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/id-audit-handoff.md:34:1. **Request to standard.** A table with one row per sentence of the system text (number them), per schema description, and per\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/io-codex.md:7:   - **Theme labels:** The change matches D38 and D404: name each outcome, without bullish or bearish labels. The schema and closing check agree.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gs-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt` and schema `candidate-schema.json`, as a design that must be READY before\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gs-handoff.md:5:any code is written. The control arm of the test has its own request and schema, `ladder/control-system.txt` and `control-schema.json`. Read `AGENTS.md` first (§1, §2, §6 and §7 govern a design, a prompt and a test). Open the code and the data behind\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gs-handoff.md:18:2. **The contract (§5.1–§5.4, the schema).** Walk these five answers through the schema, checks 1–8 and the label rule, and say what\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/in-handoff.md:11:  `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-closing.txt`; the answer schema `candidate-schema.json` in the same folder.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jd-challenge.md:24:   binding_obligation, shared_quantity, policy_stage; `clean-arch/PRD.md` §12, section 3). Over both runs: product nodes and\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mm-challenge-3.md:19:fill a new schema.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ak-challenge.md:2:- gold must_open: pos-1 credit support (binding_obligation), pos-42 big four capex (shared_quantity), pos-49 Kyber (product_node), pos-100 China H200 (policy_stage): all four opened with the right reason.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gk-codex.md:21:**(d) 对照和通过线。** v74i 原文是可用的**对照候选**，但必须固定并披露其完整请求、输入和输出格式；原生产调用还有类别、对象、开放问题及 schema，单独摘句不等于完整生产路径。([请求构造](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:377))\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ie-codex.md:3:1. **A response can stop the run before the promised refusal and resend.** [Design §5.3, check 8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:451) says exceptions other than the two named parse failures stop the run. A JSON answer containing an escaped lone surrogate such as `\"\\ud800\"` passes the schema’s non-empty string check. If it is in `object`, check 2 should refuse the unknown object and resend. Instead, [model.call](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:274) writes the parsed answer with `ensure_ascii=False`; SQLite raises `UnicodeEncodeError` before the step can check it. I reproduced the schema pass and SQLite failure in memory. The fix must specify how this response is recorded, refused and resent while preserving its text and cost, and test it through the real entry point and archive.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ie-codex.md:7:The previous review reported no new defect; its two carried-forward findings remain addressed: extreme exponents are refused and fixture 8 consistently uses `clean-99`/`v99`. All eight fixture answers passed production’s schema validator. Reading the specified checks and projections, all eight appear intended to pass and their displayed writes match; the step itself does not yet exist. I found no example that necessarily escapes all reader marks, because W permits another misleading fault to be named. The number-rule script checked 304,662 accepted samples without a changed float or rendered number.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ie-codex.md:9:**Wording:** [Check 4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:384) says a unit outside production’s list is accepted as `other`; the schema accepts the literal `other`, not an arbitrary unit string.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ie-codex.md:11:Walked the schema, eight fixture answers and projections, checks 1–8, write tables, number script, validator, and the relevant production object, bounds, date, quote and write code. **Not independently reached:** the stored input records needed to verify checks 2, 5 and 6 for fixtures 1–7, and the sealed split’s `empty_rung` implementation. Those portions of this angle remain unverified.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cg-packet-C.md:20:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cg-packet-C.md:104:- fresh-9/T1 [shared_quantity]: What will the top five hyperscale cloud companies' combined capital expenditures be in calendar 2027, against Nvidia's expectation that they approach $1.3 trillion? (period: Calendar 2027; checkable once the last of the top five hyperscalers reports fourth-quarter 2027 capital spending (early 2028). The item gives no release date for the aggregate, so the date follows the shared quantity's release.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cg-packet-C.md:177:- fresh-24/T1 [shared_quantity]: Will the Federal Reserve raise its policy rate at the September 15-16, 2026 meeting, a rate that affects financing costs for the AI infrastructure buildout underlying Nvidia's demand? (period: September 15-16, 2026 FOMC meeting.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ic-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ic-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/be-handoff.md:8:- `c9-schema.json` (every field description).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/y-challenge.md:1:Re-check after fixes (read-only). The c2 files were edited after your audit: `arms/c2-system.txt` (role clause and the CONDITION bullet), `arms/c2-closing.txt` (one sentence added after the unfiled sentence), `arms/c2-schema.json` (links and figures descriptions). You may now read `clean-arch/STEP1-CONDITIONS-DESIGN.md` §16.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/y-challenge.md:4:1. Closing check and schema \"unfiled\" against conditions: fixed (closing adds that a statement of the company's useful figures with no home keeps them and is kept as a condition; links description names both outcomes).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/y-challenge.md:9:6. Growth: system +885, closing +138, schema +1,204 characters. Reason: Alex's new conditions contract needs its definition, and field definitions sit in the schema beside the field (AGENTS §3/§6).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ls-handoff.md:20:   defect? Could change 3 (the `outcome` schema description) suppress theses c8 rightly opens, or move error to the description?\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gj-codex.md:11:- 21 条按 `shared_quantity` 或 `policy_stage` 开题，**不自动等于 21 条都应存为主题**；类型还要按具体问题判断。且只有已有当前判断、仍开放的主题才进入判断输入。([判断代码](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:76))\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iq-codex.md:7:2. **D38:** Separate company and theme fields express the intended distinction, but the current theme field accepts any nonblank name, including all five company labels. The company enum also does not by itself ensure five distinct labels or the right field for the object. The old `states` reference in `yes_no` is the direct schema-description inconsistency.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iz-challenge.md:5:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, `candidate-closing.txt`, `candidate-schema.json`,\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-B.md:20:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-B.md:78:- fresh-14/T1 [shared_quantity]: Will memory chip (DRAM and HBM) contract prices be higher at the end of calendar 2027 than at the end of calendar 2026, extending the supply shortage Micron's management expects to persist beyond 2027? (period: Calendar 2027 (next calendar year, per the shared-quantity rule); the item itself gives no price figure, only that prices have 'skyrocketed' and that Micron expects the market supply-constrained 'beyond 2027'.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-B.md:79:- fresh-14/T2 [shared_quantity]: Will the memory chip market still be supply-constrained in calendar 2027 — with DRAM/NAND contract prices above their 2026 levels — as Micron's management expects, sustaining pressure on Nvidia's memory input costs? (period: Calendar 2027; set by Micron management's forecast that the market will be supply-constrained 'beyond 2027' and checked against memory contract price releases and Micron's fiscal 2027 quarterly reports (FY2027 ends August 2027).)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-B.md:224:- fresh-22/T2 [shared_quantity]: Will industry HBM (high-bandwidth memory) shipments grow by roughly 50%-60% in calendar 2027, as the article expects, and still fall short of full demand? (period: Calendar 2027; checked against 2027 HBM shipment data published by memory-market researchers (e.g., TrendForce/DRAMeXchange) and the memory makers' disclosures during and after 2027.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-B.md:227:- fresh-22/T5 [shared_quantity]: Will HBM shipments grow by approximately 50%-60% in calendar 2027, as the article projects, and remain short of full demand? (period: Calendar 2027; checked against HBM shipment data from industry trackers (e.g., TrendForce/DRAMeXchange) and memory makers' disclosures.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/fs-codex.md:9:3. **Request construction.** The dry run passed for all 14 stored cases: **84 requests**, estimated at **$0.88**. The code checks the stored system, closing text, schema and before-state, and uses the stored sent request for c8. c12 changes the two texts; its schema file is identical to c8’s. The transport comparison is parsed-object equality, however, not the stated byte-for-byte check. [Probe code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/q12-capex-2026-11-09/q12_probe.py)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/fs-codex.md:11:4. **Before sending.** The two audit rows identify the proposed change, but do not show the required whole-request, clause-by-clause audit with a blind second reader. I found no synthetic answer run through the code checks; an unchanged schema alone does not demonstrate that check. The growth reason and character counts are recorded, but prompt-token counts are missing. The design also says 90 calls and $0.70, while the frozen probe and dry run say 84 and $0.88. [Design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/q12-capex-2026-11-09/DESIGN.md) · [Frozen probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/q12-capex-2026-11-09/probe-frozen.md)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hv-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hv-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-handoff.md:6:`c14-closing.txt` (the closing check appended after the item), `c14-schema.json` (the answer schema; production states it at the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-handoff.md:12:Task (the prompt-audit procedure, both directions): read the whole c14 request (system, closing, schema descriptions) against the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mo-slice-2.md:6:   (skipped 2/4/3, request not in the archive), enum values 43 missing 0, duplicate keys 0, one judge answer schema-refused in q3. Same kinds\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iw-handoff.md:18:  figure\"), `ladder/candidate-closing.txt` (the sentence \"For an event, check that happened…\"), `ladder/candidate-schema.json`\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iw-handoff.md:28:  schema, the checks and the view writer, with each former gap placed in a rung. The articles are in `stage_a/cases.json`.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iw-handoff.md:37:   check, every schema description): after the change, name any contradiction between them, any leftover of the retired\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iw-handoff.md:39:   place where the merger example disagrees with the schema or the code. Is anything a model needs to write a sound event\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iw-handoff.md:46:3. **What it lets through.** Give an event answer that passes the schema and every check and is wrong in a way none of the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bx-challenge.md:1:Revised c11 for both reviews (`arms/c11-closing.txt`, last paragraph; `arms/c11-schema.json`, `company_impact`):\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ar-codex.md:3:1. In [PRD §12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/PRD.md:525), the system and closing blocks match their c8 files byte for byte, including their final newline. The schema’s JSON text matches, but the PRD block has a final newline that `c8-schema.json` lacks; the parsed schemas are equal. In one stored trace request, the system matches c8 and the user message ends with exactly `\"\\n\\n\"` plus the c8 closing check. This is the stored request before the DeepSeek transport appends the schema to the system message.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gl-codex.md:5:   - **Item 1 — request and writer mapping:** The draft now supplies a request and mappings, but the contract is incomplete. It requires a date-shaped `due_day` even when `no_ladder` says to leave other fields empty, and does not specify the exact schema or how article IDs reach `created_from_input`. Two engineers could produce incompatible answers or writes. A complete fix needs the exact accepted shapes for both success and no-ladder, plus every writer input. [Design lines 153–173](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:153>); [store line 81](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:81>).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gl-codex.md:23:   `lo` and `hi` also determine ladder direction in matching, and the full-text view is read by matching search; neither reader appears in §5.4. [Matching lines 72–80 and 146](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:72>); [store lines 325–332](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:325>). The old quarterly-number check is explicitly **not rechecked**, so the new path does not meet it merely because these 34 cases lack quarterly questions. `settled_by` being present in a schema also does not prove it is nonblank, which `check_admission` requires. [Design lines 269–277](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:269>); [extraction lines 523–527 and 625–627](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:523>). Enumerate all readers and writers, and state how each old check is met or intentionally changed.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bw-codex.md:13:No specific payload was supplied for this audit, so these findings concern the request instructions and schema, not an article-specific execution.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/as-codex.md:1:The existing assertions retain their intended meaning. The fixture additions supply fields required by the adopted schema, and the two parsing changes read the same JSON payload before the appended closing check.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/as-codex.md:3:The new test separately checks the default system message, closing check, and parsed schema against c8. The reported control and two mutant results support that it catches a missing closing check and a dropped final newline; I did not rerun them.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ed-packet-F.md:20:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cp-claude.md:9:**The step** (`focused/focused_probe.py`, `system.txt`, `closing.txt`, `schema.json`):\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cp-claude.md:15:   - It is the same model and transport as Step 1: DeepSeek Flash, high effort, JSON mode with the schema in the system text.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cp-claude.md:55:**$0 checks.** A synthetic Ohio answer passes the schema and the contract. An opening without every condition and a missing decision\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cp-claude.md:94:- **$0 checks** (bytecode cleared): a right answer passes; opens false with all conditions met is refused; \"unclear\" passes the schema.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ik-audit-codex.md:9:**Key:** S = sentence within a line of the [system text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt); J = [schema description](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json); P = frozen [production prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13). “Consistent” includes output formats implementing the cited rule.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ik-audit-codex.md:36:| J19 | Refusal cases and null shape | D38, D397, D403, P16–17 | **Narrower:** repeats S6’s two unclear refusal cases. [J19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:19). |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ik-audit-codex.md:43:| J186, J197 | Numeric lower and upper bounds | P35 | Consistent with the standard; **wider than check 4**, as at S14. [J186](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:186). |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ik-audit-codex.md:46:| J246 | Reference value | D398 | Consistent with the standard; **wider than check 4**, as at S16. [J246](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:246). |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-6.md:7:   - **Missing line: confirmed.** I searched the complete stored clean request, including its schema. It has the unsigned-obligation question and 18-month check-date instruction. It also has the general same-question and “answers can move apart” instructions. I did not find an instruction equivalent to the standard’s specific boundary that an unsigned single deal can be kept separate from the plan’s amount question. This is an omission to audit, not proof that adding the sentence alone will fix the result.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-6.md:15:   Run the **$0 audit of the whole clean Step 1 request**, with the identity instructions as the first focus, against the signed standard and the observed failures. An independent blind reader should check it in both directions. Include the system text, user text, closing checks and schema descriptions, and map each failure class to its request sentence and standard line. That broader scope matters: the repository’s [prompt-audit skill](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md) and AGENTS §6 require the whole request, not only the suspected sentences.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lr-codex.md:5:**The earlier review is partly closed.** The revised plan adds the missing fourth trace segment, lists the nine cited cases, scopes both customer sentences, preserves the warning about supplier orders, removes the proposed schema change, adds several neighbouring-case controls, and specifies independent source readings and three dev draws. Those are substantive improvements. The remaining gaps are the unfinished diagnosis, the proof and comparison design, and the incomplete cost and request-size audit.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lr-codex.md:37:   The larger missing piece is the **finished diagnosis and its effect on the final answer**. A tidier question is not enough if a separately worthwhile question disappears or remains unjudged. The proposed source reading is the right next step, but the plan should complete it before declaring what goes into the combined version. Keep c8 in force and retain the year and customer changes as candidates; do not add the schema change without that evidence. D391 also asks that the expected effect on the reader or final judgement be stated and tested where possible. [D391](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4221).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ji-challenge.md:5:`unclear-schema.json`, `direction-key/brief.md`.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ji-challenge.md:10:| \"names the two readings\" invites a made-up reading when the item gives none | the sentence names the two readings they give, or says that they give none; the schema's description and the closing check say the same |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ji-challenge.md:15:| the identity check is not the bytes | checked at no cost: all 204 stored answers of the second run follow the old arm's schema in the order of their keys, at every level, and a schema with reversed keys is told apart; the probe sends through the same `model.call` path as the runner |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gm-codex.md:7:2. **The shapes and checks do not establish the claimed ladder contract.** [DESIGN.md:214](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:214), [candidate-schema.json:26](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:26). Besides reversed yes/no conditions, five company-event states can be returned worst-first and receive bullish-to-bearish labels; theme-event states can overlap; and a figure can use `n/a` as its unit or have `favourable_end: n/a` for a company. Nothing in checks 1–6 enforces those relationships. The unit enum also excludes legitimate units, such as EUR. Write the accepted combinations for all five requested shapes, specify which semantic questions remain for readers, and test examples that pass structure but are wrong. The schema alone does not enforce the exclusive null shapes; check 1 must.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bv-codex.md:3:The main conflict is that `company_impact` exists only on **new** questions, while the final check also applies when the signing question is already open. It asks the model to write the field for that open question and may then tell it to “drop that question.” Make the check work for an existing question without changing or dropping it. [Schema](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c11-schema.json:60>), [closing](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c11-closing.txt:17>).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hh-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hh-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hh-handoff.md:37:2. **The contract.** Walk every fixture of `examples.json` through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number rules. Say\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ii-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ii-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hq-audit-handoff.md:10:- the answer schema with every description: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hq-audit-handoff.md:26:  stated above it; an example must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer; the request never asks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hq-audit-handoff.md:32:1. **Request to standard.** A table with one row per sentence of the system text (number them), per schema description, and per\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-codex.md:7:`S` 为系统文本，按每行内句子顺序编号；`J` 为 schema 描述行号。`P` 为冻结提示词；`D` 为决策。下表中的“一致”包括实现标准所需的输出格式。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-codex.md:63:| J19 `no_ladder` | D38、D185、D397；P16–17 | **更宽**：同 S6.1 的旧文章年份问题。[J19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:19) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-codex.md:75:| J186 `lo` | P35；check 4 | **无来源**：数值限制同 S14.4。[J186](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:186) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-codex.md:76:| J197 `hi` | P35；check 4 | **无来源**：同上。[J197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:197) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-codex.md:80:| J246 `reference.value` | D398；check 4 | **更窄**：同 S16.1；另有同 S14.4 的代码数值限制。[J246](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:246) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-codex.md:81:| J263 `due_day_basis` | P16、26 | **更窄**：同 S22.1。[J263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:263) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-codex.md:102:并购例子逐项检查：批准且无条件、批准且有条件互斥；未决定且未撤回、未决定且已撤回互斥；被否决与前述“批准”及“未决定”互斥。按这些词的字面定义，五类覆盖批准、未决定和否决；“有条件／无条件”和“撤回／未撤回”的边界各归一类。例子没有给标签或完整答案，因此无法独立通过 schema、对象或日期检查。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/he-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/he-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/he-handoff.md:34:2. **The contract.** Walk every fixture of `examples.json` through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number rules. Say\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ia-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ia-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/b-codex.md:11:U3 requires a question even when none is sensible. Allow an explicit “none” and test that it does not manufacture a rationale. Verify the actual transmitted schema order: the property appears before `links`, but the required list places it after `links`. [U3 schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/u3-schema.json:71)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hd-codex.md:5:1. **Number preservation remains unresolved.** [DESIGN.md:292](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:292) says the request and check accept the same set, but the check receives an already-parsed float. Underflow can change a permitted nonzero number to zero; the check also accepts some values with more than fifteen significant digits. [model.py:260](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:260) confirms the parsing happens first. This is not limited to hc’s overflow example. Specify a common, enforceable number contract and parsing/storage behavior; test underflow, decimal-form integers, overflow and values on both sides of the precision boundary. The request, schema and checks must agree.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hd-codex.md:7:2. **A company figure can pass the written checks without a usable direction.** The [schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:206) permits `favourable_end: \"n/a\"` and an empty explanation for any figure. Checks 1–6 do not reject either for a company, yet [DESIGN.md:320](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:320) defines ordering only for `higher` and `lower`. Two engineers could refuse it, choose an order, or fail at runtime. Conversely, a theme can carry `higher` and a nonempty explanation. Specify and test the company/theme combinations and their refusal behavior, including the explanation, in the schema/checks and retry path.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ct-challenge.md:1:Revised for your findings: read the \"Revision\" section at the end of `council/cp-claude.md`, then re-read the whole request as the model reads it (`focused/system.txt` with `focused/schema.json` appended, the payload, then `focused/closing.txt`). Under 200 words: READY or NOT READY, with each blocking finding.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gq-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt` and schema `candidate-schema.json`, as a design that must be READY before\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gq-handoff.md:5:any code is written. The control arm of the test has its own request and schema, `ladder/control-system.txt` and `control-schema.json`. Read `AGENTS.md` first (§1, §2, §6 and §7 govern a design, a prompt and a test). Open the code and the data behind\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gq-handoff.md:18:2. **The contract (§5.1–§5.4, the schema).** Walk these five answers through the schema, checks 1–8 and the label rule, and say what\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-2.md:20:   - 更宽的数值范围更容易与专家范围重叠。因此“答对数量没下降”不能证明答案选项可靠；要同时检查范围宽度、是否覆盖所有结果、是否问了同一题，以及拒绝和无判断的数量。**没有观察到下降也不等于证明没有损失**；样本必须足以发现预先指定的、有意义的差距。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bc-codex.md:9:4. **Test.** Three Ohio draws and folding controls are a useful initial probe, not an adequate proof of a general fix. Name the control articles and expected questions in advance; include small unsigned obligations, already signed components, duplicate descriptions, and genuinely independent large unsigned obligations in other industries. Use stored requests with their actual prior questions, and have a blind reader compare each answer with its source. Verify no-cost request and schema checks and preflight first; measure wording and token changes. Two successes in three would show a possible effect, not establish reliability or the share of the broader failure class fixed. The claimed class is one gold entry, not a census of all folding failures.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/he-codex.md:9:3. **Malformed and schema-invalid answers have no defined Stage A outcome.** [DESIGN.md:344](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:344) retries refusals by checks 1–6, and [line 613](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:613) names three outcomes. But [model.py:258](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:258) raises `SchemaError` before those checks for malformed or schema-invalid answers. Two engineers could stop the measurement or count and retry the answer differently. Define both first and second failures, the archive record, denominator and report, and test them. Also specify what happens when the archived response is truncated: [model.py:276](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:276) limits it to 200,000 characters, while the proposed exact-number check rereads it.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lr-handoff.md:20:   defect? Could change 3 (the `outcome` schema description) suppress theses c8 rightly opens, or move error to the description?\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hn-codex.md:11:**Fixture walk.** All eight answers passed the actual production schema validator. The remaining checks and writes are not built, so these are design-level results:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hn-codex.md:24:For enforcement: the validator covers schema types and required fields, but not the five-item maximum. Checks 1–6 require the new step’s stated checks; production’s `resolve`, date helpers and quote repair provide parts of them. Production’s `check_bounds` does not enforce the open lower end or exact-decimal comparisons. Check 7’s rendering and ordering and check 8’s retry and record are new behavior. The long-integer case above is the enforcement gap I found.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hn-codex.md:28:Walked §5.3–5.4, all eight fixture answers and displayed projections, the schema, number rule, and the named production code. **Not reached:** the individual source and reader-answer rows in `dryrun/`, `dryrun2/packet-a`, `dryrun3/`–`dryrun8/`, and `reference/`; therefore I have not independently verified the fixtures’ claims about those readings.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hs-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hs-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ah-handoff.md:3:Scope: the complete request c8 as the model reads it: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-system.txt` (system), `c8-closing.txt` (appended after the item), `c8-schema.json` (stated in the system text, every field description included).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-challenge-4.md:16:   standard's same-question test (§4: \"同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题；答案能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注的，才是另一题\") and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gt-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt` and schema `candidate-schema.json`, as a design that must be READY before\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gt-handoff.md:5:any code is written. The control arm of the test has its own request and schema, `ladder/control-system.txt` and `control-schema.json`. Read `AGENTS.md` first (§1, §2, §6 and §7 govern a design, a prompt and a test). Open the code and the data behind\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gt-handoff.md:18:2. **The contract (§5.1–§5.4, the schema).** Walk these five answers through the schema, checks 1–8 and the label rule, and say what\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gu-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt` and schema `candidate-schema.json`, as a design that must be READY before\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gu-handoff.md:5:any code is written. The control arm of the test has its own request and schema, `ladder/control-system.txt` and `control-schema.json`. Read `AGENTS.md` first (§1, §2, §6 and §7 govern a design, a prompt and a test). Open the code and the data behind\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gu-handoff.md:18:2. **The contract (§5.1–§5.4, the schema).** Walk these five answers through the schema, checks 1–8 and the label rule, and say what\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gr-codex.md:3:1. **The comparison can reward an invalid refusal.** [DESIGN.md:220](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:220) accepts any nonblank `no_ladder` reason. For example, the model can say “nothing is checkable” for a plainly dated approval question. Readers mark only written ladders, so nobody judges whether that refusal was justified. Lines 1–3 can pass with zero candidate ladders; the minimum-population rule only partly limits this. The control also has a vague refusal instruction and a mandatory event `year` that the candidate does not have to produce ([control schema:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/control-schema.json:29)). A complete test needs common eligibility, reader assessment of refusals in both versions, and an explicit account of the control’s extra event-year burden. This leaves **gq finding 2** only partly answered.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gr-codex.md:7:3. **The reader may see ranges without the reference that explains them.** The request asks for ranges near, above and below an expectation, but [DESIGN.md:251](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:251) renders only intervals and stores the reference separately. The frozen judge sees rung labels and conditions, not that separate record ([judging.py:121](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:121)). This also omits v74i’s instruction to state the neutral comparison in its condition. Specify exactly what each condition says and how the judge receives the reference, or explicitly assess the loss against the frozen judge. For a numeric reference, the schema also allows `value: null`; check 6 only checks a value **if present**.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/id-audit-codex.md:3:以下 `S` 指[系统文本](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt)，编号为文件行号及行内句序；`J` 指 [schema 描述](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json)，数字为行号；`P` 指[冻结生产提示词](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13)。以下“一致”包含有来源的输出格式。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/id-audit-codex.md:69:| J197 `hi` | P35；检查4 | **部分无投资标准来源**：同上。[J197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:197) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/id-audit-codex.md:73:| J246 `reference.value` | D398；检查4 | **部分无投资标准来源**：同数字限制。[J246](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:246) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/id-audit-codex.md:74:| J263 `due_day_basis` | P16、26 | **更窄**：同 S22。[J263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:263) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/go-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt` and schema `candidate-schema.json`, as a design that must be READY before\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/go-handoff.md:18:2. **The contract (§5.1–§5.4, the schema).** Walk these five answers through the schema, checks 1–8 and the label rule, and say what\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jh-challenge.md:15:   company\"; `unclear-closing.txt`, the last check; `unclear-schema.json`): the favourable end is taken from the topic first,\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gs-codex.md:13:**The five paths**, assuming each passes the schema and applicable checks: company yes/no writes the supplied Yes and No conditions; company states are stored in the five business-label order; theme states retain their distinct names and input order; a company figure is sorted and labelled from its favourable end, with the quoted reference appended to the middle condition; a theme figure without a reference is sorted, with each interval used as both label and condition. A refusal by checks 1 or 3–6 is retried once; check 2 ends without retry. The common dates, object and record fields are written as described in [§5.4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:304).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-handoff.md:10:- the answer schema with every description: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-handoff.md:24:  stated above it; an example must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer; the request never asks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-handoff.md:29:1. **Request to standard.** A table with one row per sentence of the system text (number them), per schema description, and per\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ir-handoff.md:8:The arm, in `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/` (`candidate-system.txt`, `candidate-closing.txt`, `candidate-schema.json`), is the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ir-handoff.md:9:request as first sent (`probe-2026-11-10/sent-system.txt`, `sent-closing.txt`, `sent-schema.json`) with exactly these changes:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ir-handoff.md:18:1. First line: \"send\", or \"hold\" with the exact words or schema change you would make.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ir-handoff.md:19:2. Is the arm exactly what D407 describes: nothing more in the system text, the closing check or the schema than the four points?\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ir-handoff.md:20:3. Is the request consistent with its schema (every field the text names exists; no text about a field that is gone)?\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cq-codex.md:14:3. **Code contract.** It checks the schema, decision coverage, necessary opening conditions, shown IDs, and statement membership. It still accepts `opens: false` when all conditions are met, empty new questions, repeated question IDs, and separate questions for statements about the same obligation. It does not check whether a cited existing question actually asks about that obligation, or whether the new question is valid and publicly settleable. Those require reading the answers; ID membership alone is insufficient.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cq-codex.md:18:5. **Interpretability.** The runner silently skips planned cases with no routed statements, and schema failures are recorded without the raw answer. Report skipped cases and preserve failed responses so missing results cannot look like successful exclusions. The company-impact explanation can also disagree with the opening decision, as §53 already observed.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jd-codex.md:22:一个存档反例是 `u1/clean-9`：它标为 `shared_quantity`，问中国企业的 AI 加速器预算中多少给国内产品。第一段的请求只允许使用给定的主题；第一次测试中，两家读者都接受过“没有合适主题，因此拒绝判断”的答案。直接把所有 `shared_quantity` 指向某个主题，会替它指定一个不覆盖该问题的对象。见 [原始案例](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/cases.json)。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gx-codex.md:19:   - The schema’s `not_judged` description says it is empty when the topic “asks about one thing,” which can conflict with an omitted condition on that thing ([schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:53)).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gx-codex.md:21:   Complete the required clause-by-clause audit of the revised request and schema in both directions before a send ([design](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:226)).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gx-codex.md:25:**Prior review and control.** Version 14 answers gv’s refusal-list mismatch, figure order, numeric failure handling, empty stability population, zero denominators and reference-label overstatement. It acknowledges rather than repairs the two unsound state examples; B4 was reread on the familiar packet, with fresh planted tests still ahead. The audit’s omissions are mostly addressed, except the narrowed refusal and schema wording above.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-challenge-5.md:23:   identity sentences against the standard's identity rules (§4 \"同一题、续期，还是另一题\" whole, and §3's \"同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iw-codex.md:15:4. **请求和读者表把“更细区别都不判”写得比决定宽。** [candidate-system.txt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt:13) 与 [stage-a-reader-brief.md](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/stage-a-reader-brief.md:33) 要求把结果内的细分放入 `not_judged`；而同一请求第 5 行及 [schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:50) 只要求列出**题目措辞中**被遗漏的部分。普通的无条件批准题并未提及附条件批准：按前者要列，按后者允许空列表。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iw-codex.md:17:   D409 举出的附条件批准是可不单独判的细分，并没有授权把被追踪的主要结果本身丢掉。[u1/clean-12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/three_outcomes_by_hand.py:39) 的原始结果同时追踪调查结论及罚款或补救；手写题只问是否罚款或补救。“调查结束、没有处罚”与“调查仍未结束”虽有区分，但结论的内容被丢掉，也没有作为遗漏列出。三档能表达是否处罚，不能同时完整表达原结果中调查结论的内容。需先对照 D409 与原题确定什么可以列为不判，统一请求、schema 和表格。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iw-codex.md:44:10. [candidate-system.txt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt:13) 的“第三种加到你的答案里；不要写它”容易让模型以为必须在 JSON 中提供第三项。实际 schema 只收 `happened` 和 `ruled_out`，第三档由代码写入。并且 `ruled_out: null` 时只生成两档，schema 的“第三种由代码加入”应明确限定为有否决条件时。合并案例本身的两个字段符合 schema，未发现要求填写已退役的五状态或 yes/no 形状。发生和否决的定义在正文、schema 与末尾检查重复；末尾复核是有意的检查，schema 与正文重复可以精简，但要保留一致含义。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mo-challenge-2.md:24:Exceptions inside the judge's own replay (refused twice, schema, transport) keep the internal redo, as you said.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mo-challenge-2.md:28:shows an eligible failure (a transport failure after its retries, an answer refused or not fitting its schema), otherwise the run stops;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lm-codex.md:9:4. **Retry handling — closed for the reported cases.** The probe retries output-limit cuts, malformed JSON and schema failures, but returns without retrying a later validation failure. That matches the production sequence ([probe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/probe_c14.py:103); [runner](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/runner.py:309)). The record reports a fake-transport check for a cut answer, duplicate ID, refusal and valid answer; it is a reported result, not a saved test I independently ran ([preflight record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/preflight-c14.output.txt:41)).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-codex.md:5:File references below use [the frozen standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:271), [the c14 system text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:1), [the closing check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-closing.txt:1), and [the schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-schema.json:1).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-codex.md:19:| Four opening reasons are a closed set, with no company annual main-driver category. Financial measures cannot open “on [their] own.” [System 89–90, 116–120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:89); [schema 49–57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-schema.json:49) | **Keeps narrower** | The standard explicitly permits the annual measure carrying a company’s value, such as a key segment’s revenue, for the company’s current or next fiscal year. It also permits proposing another company’s own measure subject to the tests. The schema cannot express that opening reason. [Standard 276, 292–297](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:276) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-codex.md:29:| A new question must have an answer that can move apart from the closest open question. [System 122–124](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:122); [closing 15](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-closing.txt:15); [schema 64–77](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-schema.json:64) | **Keeps wider / incomplete** | Answers moving apart is necessary, but the standard also asks whether that difference makes a genuinely different business judgment and whether an analyst would bet separately. The request mentions a separate bet, but does not clearly apply the standard’s counterfactual test; the deadline exception shows why movement alone is insufficient. [Standard 310–316, 345, 348](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:310) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-codex.md:30:| Proposed question’s `period` is “the period or check date that settles” it. [Schema 38–47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-schema.json:38) | **Keeps narrower / ambiguous** | A quantity’s covered period and its publication date are different things. The schema supplies one field described as either, although the standard uses the period to identify the quantity and the release date to settle it. [Standard 279, 302–305](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:279) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-codex.md:31:| Evidence summary and evidence period preserve the source’s period; missing periods remain unknown. [System 138–146, 169–170](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:138); [schema 106–108, 261–270](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-schema.json:106) | **Consistent** | The standard requires the period described by the statement and warns against turning the remainder of a year into the whole year. [Standard 416](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:416) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jy-codex.md:5:3. The typed paragraph, closing sentence and schema are consistent with the two adopted rules. The code still checks only that the two typed strings are nonempty; the full reading must assess their meaning. The registered D420 stop allows one missing ruling out in nine, even though D420 calls each such answer faulty. It also lacks the earlier probe’s minimum number of readable French event ladders: declines could leave the D420 check unexercised.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iy-challenge.md:5:`candidate-schema.json`, `ladder_step.py` (`event_rungs`), `stage-a-reader-brief.md`; `stage_a/collect_readings.py`\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iy-challenge.md:19:| 10. \"is added to your answer: do not write it\" may be read as a third item to supply | reworded: \"You write these two conditions and no other: what is left, neither of the two, needs no condition\"; the schema's description says no condition is written for what is left |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iy-codex.md:19:10. **已关闭。** “You write these two conditions and no other: what is left … needs no condition”（[candidate-system.txt:13](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt:13)）与 [schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:91) 的“No condition is written for what is left”一致，不再要求模型写第三个字段。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iy-codex.md:24:- “every way”出现在正文、schema 描述和末尾检查中，共三次；读者表却使用较窄的“plain ways”。末尾复核有其用途，但三个位置需要表达同一范围。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iy-codex.md:25:- 正文要求模型写两个条件，同时允许 `ruled_out` 为 null；schema 接受 null，整体可理解，但“two conditions”宜写清第二个可以为空。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iy-codex.md:26:- 没发现请求仍要求模型输出退役的 `yes_no` 或五状态字段，也没发现合并例子要求 schema 或代码拒绝的字段。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hc-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hc-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hc-handoff.md:34:2. **The contract.** Walk every fixture of `examples.json` through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number rules. Say\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/a-handoff.md:8:- the request: `clean-arch/takeover-2026-11-07/k6b-system.txt`, `k6b-closing.txt`, `k6b-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bl-handoff.md:6:- c10a: `arms/c10a-system.txt`, `c10a-closing.txt`, `c10a-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bl-handoff.md:7:- c10b: `arms/c10b-system.txt`, `c10b-closing.txt`, `c10b-schema.json` (with the `unsigned_obligation` field description).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jh-codex.md:9:- **G1：不能可靠判断参考修改是否使方向变差。** 15 次中相差三次只是 **20 个百分点的观察差**，这组很小、又按此前表现挑选；没有定义采样误差或逐题分布。总数还可能掩盖一题向高、另一题向低的变化。`acc/clean-1` 和 `acc/clean-7` 也未进入 G1 的五题统计。最便宜的修正是逐题报告两个请求的三次结果、拒绝和无法解析的次数，把差异标为探索性信号；不要把“小于两次”称为未显示影响，更不能据此证明安全。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iq-handoff.md:11:`round3-closing.txt`, `round3-schema.json`):\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iq-handoff.md:12:- `candidate-schema.json`: two new first fields, `named` (every figure or event the topic's outcome names) and `main` (the main\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iq-handoff.md:23:1. First line: \"send\", or \"hold\" with the exact words or the exact schema change you would make.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iq-handoff.md:26:3. Is anything in the request now inconsistent with the schema (a field named in one and not the other; an instruction that the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iq-handoff.md:27:   schema cannot hold)?\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-challenge-10.md:7:  Step 1's request says \"shared_quantity: … for this or next calendar year\" and \"A thesis asks one quantity for one period\"; D417 confirmed the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cs-challenge.md:1:Revised for your findings: read the \"Revision\" section at the end of `council/cp-claude.md`, then the current `focused/closing.txt`, `focused/schema.json` and `check()` and `send()` in `focused/focused_probe.py`. Under 200 words: is anything still blocking? End with SEND, SEND WITH CHANGES, or DO NOT SEND.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ca-challenge.md:1:Revised `company_impact` (`arms/c11-schema.json`) for the auditor's blocker: \"judged against the company's size as the item states it,\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hk-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hk-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cd-challenge.md:1:Revised `company_impact` once more (`arms/c11-schema.json`) for the design blocker: \"Write no figure the item does not give; this field\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ih-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ih-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hp-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schem