p1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hm-audit-handoff.md:26:  stated above it; an example must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer; the request never asks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hm-audit-handoff.md:32:1. **Request to standard.** A table with one row per sentence of the system text (number them), per schema description, and per\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ib-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ib-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hu-codex.md:15:**Walked in full:** Stage A’s six lines, accounting table and shares; every field of the form against the request and schema; the prior Stage A findings. **Not walked in full:** the individual stored practice and reference answers and their counting scripts; their stated counts are assigned to the separate evidence reviewer.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hx-codex.md:5:I ran all eight answers through production’s `model.check_schema`: all eight passed. Checks 1–8 are not implemented yet, so their results below are a reading of the design, not a run of the step.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hx-codex.md:18:The [schema validator](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:179) enforces the declared types, required fields, patterns and enums; it does not enforce exactly five entries. The design assigns that and the other cross-field rules to new checks. Production’s [bounds check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) alone does not establish an open lower end or exact-decimal comparisons; the design explicitly adds both. The [write table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:517) is consistent with the displayed projections I walked.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/io-handoff.md:10:- The request as first sent: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/probe-2026-11-10/sent-system.txt`, `sent-closing.txt`, `sent-schema.json`.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/io-handoff.md:12:  `candidate-schema.json`. Diff them yourself; besides the three changes, the closing check and three schema descriptions\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/io-handoff.md:24:   other sentence of the request, the schema or the closing check?\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gr-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt` and schema `candidate-schema.json`, as a design that must be READY before\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gr-handoff.md:5:any code is written. The control arm of the test has its own request and schema, `ladder/control-system.txt` and `control-schema.json`. Read `AGENTS.md` first (§1, §2, §6 and §7 govern a design, a prompt and a test). Open the code and the data behind\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gr-handoff.md:18:2. **The contract (§5.1–§5.4, the schema).** Walk these five answers through the schema, checks 1–8 and the label rule, and say what\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ha-codex.md:13:5. **The before-build and before-send instructions conflict.** [§10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:782) still requires Alex’s word and calls the lines proposed. [D400 and D401](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4376) have already settled those points. Meanwhile, the audit of the **current** request and schema is required before a send, but has not yet been done ([§5.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:258)). Update the stale gate and complete the blind audit before the authorized send.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ha-codex.md:19:- **Request sources:** The principal question, object, date, reference and direction clauses have entries in [§5.2’s source table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:213); the event-date restriction is explicitly narrower. The closing check repeats preceding rules, and I found no covered-company or test-article example in the system text. I have **not completed a sentence-by-sentence independent audit of every schema description against its original source**; the required current-version audit remains open.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-handoff.md:10:- the answer schema with every description: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-handoff.md:26:  stated above it; an example must agree with the standard, the schema and the code that reads the answer; the request never asks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hi-audit-handoff.md:32:1. **Request to standard.** A table with one row per sentence of the system text (number them), per schema description, and per\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/go-codex.md:3:1. **The request, schema and checks disagree.** [candidate-system.txt:6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt:6) rejects every quarterly or half-year figure and every figure beyond next year. [Check 5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:230) applies the quarter check only to company figures and exempts binding obligations from the year limit, as [production does](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:625). The schema’s [no-ladder description](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:19) mentions only an undated topic, omitting the other allowed reasons. The closing check asks a reference with a value to fall in the middle range, although an event can have a numeric reference and no ranges. Specify the accepted cases consistently across all three surfaces, including the obligation exception.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/go-codex.md:21:6. **Request audit.** Against the cited sources, I read the opening, lines 4–5, 9, 12, 14–15, 17 and 20–23 as consistent, subject to the conflicts above. Line 6 is narrower than the implemented exceptions; line 13 leaves three- or four-state events unrepresentable as distinct states; line 16 extends the figure-specific D398 treatment to event references. The closing check adds the numeric-reference-for-an-event problem above. The examples do not name the covered company or obviously reproduce a test article. The schema descriptions and the unwritten control request still need the complete blind audit promised in [§5.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:191).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/go-codex.md:23:7. **gn’s findings.** Version 6 answers the selected-send, total control denominator, no-main-part, `outcome` precedence, year/reference-value marks, concurrent-call handling, switch, ordering and due-guard findings in text. It narrows the reference-only judgement rule correctly. The remaining gaps are the control’s assessability, workload budget, request/schema/check agreement, and the calendar-day and crash details above. The prior path wording is corrected.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ju-challenge.md:4:`survey-schema.json` (`no_ladder`, its description).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ju-challenge.md:6:- The survey arm's schema now lists the seventh reason as its request does (`run.py check`: the arm differs from the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ju-challenge.md:7:  control in the system text and the schema).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/il-codex.md:5:I would change the event clause in both the request and schema to:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-challenge-3.md:5:§3 table, §3 \"问题怎么写\", §4 \"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"). Attack the verdicts, not only the summary: a \"B\" that is really an allowed\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lt-handoff.md:6:`c15-closing.txt` (the closing check appended after the item), `c15-schema.json` (the answer schema; production states it at the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lt-handoff.md:7:end of the system text). The previous version is `c8-*` in the same folder; c15 changes four sentences and one schema field description (diff all three files).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lt-handoff.md:12:Task (the prompt-audit procedure, both directions): read the whole c14 request (system, closing, schema descriptions) against the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gn-codex.md:11:   The request allows a signed obligation beyond 18 months; check 5 refuses every binding obligation. It permits a quarterly company figure and a figure beyond next year without stating the corresponding refusals. Its closing check introduces “after the item’s day” and “on or after … settling material is published” without stating those rules above it. Align the complete request, schema and checks with the applicable sources; identify deliberate production-check departures rather than presenting conflicting instructions as compatible. [DESIGN.md:221](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:221), [v74i:13](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gn-codex.md:13:   Sentence audit: the opening role and fixed-ladder instruction, lines 4, 9, 12, 14–15, 17 and the fiscal/date portions of 20–22 are consistent with their cited sources, subject to the conflicts above. Line 5 is narrower than D397; line 6 omits its no-main-part case. Line 13 requires exactly five event states, which is narrower than a real event with three or four possible outcomes and needs an explanation of how those outcomes are represented. Line 16’s reference and estimated ranges follow D398, but its treatment of an event’s reference is wider than D398’s figure-specific implementation. Line 22’s event-year convention has no source in the cited table. The closing check adds the date rules above. The drug, carrier and spending examples do not name the covered company or obviously reproduce a test article. A complete audit must also cover the schema descriptions and the still-unwritten control request.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gn-codex.md:25:   Another passing wrong answer is a **2027 question with `year` set to 2026**: the schema requires only nonblank text, and the year check does not verify agreement with the question. The judge is shown that incorrect year. Likewise, a reference quote can say “$10 billion” while `value` is 20 billion: check 6 verifies the quote and the middle-range position, but not that the value represents the quote. Add both to the reader checks and specify what code can establish. [candidate-schema.json:54](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:54), [judging.py:123](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:123).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/fs-handoff.md:23:4. **Anything missing before the send?** The prompt audit rows, a synthetic answer (the schema is unchanged, so the code checks\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lv-codex.md:7:I compared both candidates with c8 and read the full c15yc system text, closing check and schema together. The schema is unchanged in both candidates. The changed text names no company, product or benchmark case and is general across industries.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lv-codex.md:22:- The disputed schema changes are absent from both candidates.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bd-handoff.md:7:  same for the closing and schema files;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ac-handoff.md:3:Scope: the candidate request c7: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c7-system.txt`, `c7-closing.txt`, `c7-schema.json`. Diff against c6 (`arms/c6-*`); only section 3 of the system text, one closing sentence and two schema fields changed.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lj-handoff.md:11:- the changed request: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt`, `c14-closing.txt`, `c14-schema.json` against\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/il-challenge.md:7:   that neither the topic nor the item gives a date and the topic names no period\". The schema's `no_ladder` description and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/il-challenge.md:9:   `candidate-schema.json`'s `no_ladder` description again.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ac-codex.md:15:- **Closing check — contradicts** the permitted analyst-set dates and can apply the overbroad bans. Its closest-question test also gives no clear pass when the open list is empty; the schema explicitly permits `null` then.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ir-codex.md:1:hold — Remove this sentence from the `theme_states.name` schema description: “Never Strongly bullish, Bullish, Neutral, Bearish or Strongly bearish: those are a company's labels.”\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ir-codex.md:5:2. **The request and schema are consistent.** The fields named in the text exist in the schema, and the text does not refer to a removed field.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gz-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json` and worked examples `examples.json`, as a\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gz-handoff.md:23:3. **The contract (§5, the schema, the examples).** Walk the examples through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/dm-packet-E.md:20:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ig-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ig-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/is-codex.md:21:- The four-range test allows its schema assertion to pass regardless of the result ([test_ladder_step.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/test_ladder_step.py:133)). The count tests also do not exercise the resend path promised in the design.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gv-codex.md:3:1. **The refusal test uses a different rule from the request.** The request permits five reasons for `no_ladder` ([request, line 6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt:6)). Stage A instead imports the longer list from [reader brief A, line 25](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/dryrun2/reader-brief-a.md:25), which also accepts executive appointments, buybacks and other cases. A model can therefore disobey the request and still be counted as **right** under [design, lines 563–573](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:563). Make the request, schema, reader form and success measure use the same settled cases; exercise each allowed and disallowed refusal. The second dry run expressly did **not** exercise the added cases ([line 464](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:464)).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gv-codex.md:15:7. **The request audit remains incomplete.** Against the cited table: lines 1, 4–5, 9, 12, 15–17 and 20–23 broadly follow their stated sources; line 6 follows the listed exclusions but conflicts with the reader form above; line 13 is narrower for events naturally having three or four states; line 14 adds `other` to production’s units; line 25 repeats the rules but three sampled outcomes cannot prove complete coverage. The request permits another company or unlisted theme, which check 2 deliberately turns into no view ([design, line 228](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:228)). The required blind audit of **every schema description and example**, in both directions against its sources and checks, is still explicitly open ([line 674](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:674)).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/af-handoff.md:13:- Step 1 prompt `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c7-system.txt`, `c7-closing.txt`, `c7-schema.json`; settings DeepSeek Flash,\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bd-claude.md:26:**Size.** System 15,828 → 16,663 (+835), closing +6, schema +2. The reason is the two definitions the measured failures lacked; no\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bd-claude.md:93:  - a synthetic c9 answer for the Ohio case (a signing thesis, linked with the aggregate) passes the schema and runner checks, its\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bd-claude.md:96:  schema: 395 judged, 0 schema or contract refusals, none skipped.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bd-claude.md:99:  - c9 adds 980 characters (the schema is stated in the system text). That is about 212 prompt tokens, +2.5%, an estimate from\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/x-codex.md:3:The audit covers the system, closing check and schema. Compared with K6b, c2 adds financial figures and conditions, removes financial quantities from its opening examples, and broadens the ban on opening a financial measure. The closing check is unchanged. Sources: [standard §§4–5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:308), [Alex’s rulings](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:312), and [his reframe](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:444).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/x-codex.md:9:- **Unfiled and conditions** (system 7–10, 53–62; closing 15; [schema 189–194](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c2-schema.json:189)): the condition exception is **consistent** with Alex’s §17 amendment to D209. Unqualified “unfiled” in the closing check and schema **contradicts** it. The definition “financial performance” **keeps narrower** than his “useful company financial figure”; its cash/funding test has **no source** as a general rule. Figure fields preserve measure, period, value, kind and basis, consistent with §17’s attribution and period intent; the surrounding evidence supplies attribution.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/x-codex.md:11:- **Closing reject rows** (closing 3–11): background, generic claims, specifications, political stance, unrelated companies, repeats and boilerplate are **mostly consistent** with §5.3. The valuation row is **consistent** with §5.3’s conditional-valuation rule, but **contradicts** Alex’s specific target-price ruling when its assumptions, derivation and date are present. The “do not drop” retold actual figure clause **keeps wider** than §5.3, where an identifiable retold past actual is optional. The schema’s empty-link definition repeats the condition conflict.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/x-codex.md:19:- **Reframe:** an unlinked useful figure may be kept, but the evidence test, closing 15 and schema pull against it. A question without an expressed reason can still open.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/x-codex.md:23:Before a send: align the closing check and schema with conditions; resolve the target-price conflict against Alex’s ruling and the standard; require a source-backed view with a reason and the standard’s checkable outcome; narrow the borrowing ban; replace the cash-specific shortcut with a general usefulness test. Recheck the complete request and its size afterward. These are audit recommendations, not edits.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bl-codex.md:14:- **Separate-bet instruction and schema:** “If the two cannot move apart” and `why_a_separate_bet` **keep narrower** when applied to D388 without an exception. The schema requires that explanation even for the signing question.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/fb-codex.md:9:4. **Bounds and configuration.** Step 1 has per-run call, time and estimated-cost limits; they are not a shared cap across all draws and stages. Step 2 and judging do not use that budget. Output paths are caller-supplied without folder containment. The default Step 1 path is documented and tested as c8, but candidate prompt and schema arguments can override it; no Stage 2 launcher shown here pins or verifies the invocation.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lq-handoff.md:20:   defect? Could change 3 (the `outcome` schema description) suppress theses c8 rightly opens, or move error to the description?\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hj-codex.md:11:**Fixture walk.** All eight answers passed the actual `model.check_schema`. The remaining checks and writes do not yet exist, so the following are *design-level walks*, not executions of the proposed step:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hj-codex.md:24:**Checks 1–8.** The schema enforces required keys, types, enums and nonblank patterned text; production’s validator does not enforce maximum array lengths. Checks 1–6 therefore need new code for the stated shape, object, state, number, date and reference rules. The named production functions support object resolution, date limits, quote repair and parts of range validation; `check_bounds` alone does not enforce an open lower end, and the proposed check must compare exact decimals. Check 7’s ordering and rendering are new behavior derived from the named split code. Check 8’s retry and complete outcome record are also new: `model.call` raises on malformed or schema-invalid output but does not perform this step’s retry. The quotation choice and number-check defect above are the places where the specified enforcement is not yet sufficient.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hj-codex.md:30:Walked all eight fixture answers and their displayed writes, checks 1–8, the schema and number rule; I did not execute the unbuilt checks or verify full database writes.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/iu-codex.md:28:- **acc/clean-8，第 1、3 次，XR：模型错误，且字段表达能力不足。** 文章写预计出货增长“approximately 50%-60%”；答案保留了原句，却把数值设为空，显示“no reference figure”。[输出结构]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json )只允许一个数字或空值，不能直接表达这一区间。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hf-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hf-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hf-handoff.md:34:2. **The contract.** Walk every fixture of `examples.json` through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number rules. Say\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ah-codex.md:3:I read the three files in order, including every schema description. This is a read-only request audit; I did not read `council/ah-claude.md` or inspect model answers.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ah-codex.md:19:   - **Missing from the request:** §4 requires a candidate to explain *which* revenue, profit, cash/credit risk or competitive position changes; “can change a position” does not make that test explicit. §3 also says one question asks one quantity for one period or one event; the schema does not say so. The closing rejection of a thesis with no settlement date conflicts with the system’s “otherwise use null”: rewriting an unsupported question is