ppress a correct opening, split one event incorrectly, or simply move the extra phrase into `description`, which remains a free-text question. The proposed test checks the outcome’s shape and an aggregate opening count; it does not establish that the original question, its meaningful alternatives, and any independently worthwhile second question survive. The existing request already states the one-quantity/one-event rule, so adding it again in the schema is a hypothesis about where the model needs it, not a demonstrated root cause. [c8 system prompt, lines 85–90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-system.txt:85), [c8 schema, lines 30–36](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-schema.json:30).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lq-codex.md:37:   - The stated **$2** for the third proof is a substantial probe, not a few cents. Show the call count, input/output-token assumptions, retries, reader costs and total including both arms and the fresh/dev work. First identify the smallest stored cases that can decide whether the schema wording helps. [AGENTS.md, lines 345–353](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:345).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lq-codex.md:41:   Keep the year and customer collision as candidates, after correcting the census and restoring the relevant controls. Keep the second-thing class in the diagnosis, but **do not present the schema wording as a settled fix yet**. First separate genuinely independent questions from references, alternatives and context; trace representative stored answers to why Step 1 wrote them; then define a small proof that checks what the reader can actually have judged.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gi-handoff.md:37:  (`check_ladder`, `normalise_ladder`, `check_bounds`, `check_admission`, the candidate schema), `src/hivemind/views/writing.py`\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gi-handoff.md:39:- The clean path: `clean-arch/PRD.md` §§4–7 and §12 (the c8 schema: a new thesis carries description, outcome, period, opens_as,\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gj-challenge.md:17:   shared_quantity 13, policy_stage 8; period null 0, with an ISO date 5, prose only 29.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gj-challenge.md:52:3. **Answer (strict schema):** either a ladder — `settles` (the one number or one event), `left_out` (parts of the thesis's wording\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gj-challenge.md:66:9. **Model:** `gpt-6-luna` with the strict schema at medium effort (the judge's setting), one configuration.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cx-packet-D.md:20:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/im-challenge.md:3:Your clause is now in the request, word for word, and the schema's `no_ladder` description and the readers' form say the same.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hz-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hz-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hx-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hx-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hx-handoff.md:36:## Your angle: the contract (design §5.3; the field-by-field writes at the head of §5.4; `ladder/examples.json`; `ladder/candidate-schema.json`; `ladder/number_rule_check.py`)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hx-handoff.md:41:1. Walk **each of the eight fixtures** of `examples.json` through the schema (with production's validator, `model.check_schema`\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ij-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ij-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/y-codex.md:3:1. **DISAGREE.** The new closing sentence and schema description clarify what happens to a useful figure with no home. But [system 55–57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c2-system.txt:55) says a statement of company financial figures “lists them,” while the schema says to list *useful* figures. More importantly, the record can still contain unwanted material alongside a useful figure.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/y-codex.md:13:6. **DISAGREE on the count.** The current character differences are system **+885**, closing **+138**, schema **+1,717**. The stated need explains growth, but not why every addition is needed or what was cut.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jt-challenge.md:11:on a typed one; tests `test_d416_*`); a hand-written typed answer passes its schema, the checks and the view writer.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jt-challenge.md:14:1. Each arm's text as the model reads it, whole (AGENTS §6): the typed event paragraph and its schema descriptions and\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-6.md:16:3. **探针的目标和通过线需要重写。** 两份 `u3/clean-11` 答案不是两个独立题目；对同一题重新发送三次，不能再按两题计入“修好三题”。而且，“四个正确拒绝允许一个变成可判断”可能容许 **25% 的对照退步**。其中一些对照的正确性还存在读者分歧，不能都称为确定正确。[追踪结果](</Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/stage-a-trace/STAGE-A-TRACE-RESULT.md>)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ar-handoff.md:7:- `clean-arch/PRD.md` §12: its introduction, \"System prompt\", \"Closing check\" and \"Structured-output schema\";\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ar-handoff.md:11:1. Do PRD §12's three blocks equal `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-system.txt`, `c8-closing.txt` and `c8-schema.json`\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ar-handoff.md:15:2. Do the test changes only bring fixtures to the adopted schema and parse the payload before the closing check, leaving every\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bk-handoff.md:8:  and the same for `c10b-closing.txt` and `c10b-schema.json`;\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gz-codex.md:17:   Complete fix: resolve each allowed-but-dropped or refused answer, including the no-expectation event, and audit the **revised** system text, schema descriptions and examples both ways before a send. The company/theme identification, one-question rule, units, reference and date clauses otherwise largely follow the sources listed in [§5.2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:198). The event-date restriction is narrower than v74i and is explicitly acknowledged there.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cr-codex.md:4:- **Narrower — signing status.** The [required choices](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/focused/schema.json:28) have no “unknown” option. If an article describes a guarantee but does not say whether it was signed, the model must claim it was signed, claim it was not, or say it is not an obligation.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cr-codex.md:6:- **Wider — date.** The [schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/focused/schema.json:82) permits any check date within 18 months; [c8 §3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-system.txt:104) first requires the date supported by the item.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lo-codex.md:5:2. **Standard preflight — run and recorded.** The record reports exit 0. Its output shows 170 matching records judged, none refused, and two skipped because their requests were absent from the archive. It also reports two schema-refused answers and 12 extraction items dropped; the output does not establish by itself whether any refusal needs diagnosis under §5. The separate clean-Step-1 replay reports 24 answers passed and none skipped. [Standard output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/scripts-preflight.output.txt:3), [c14 record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/preflight-c14.output.txt:26), [§5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:174).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lo-codex.md:9:4. **Whole-request audit — not yet demonstrated.** The blind reader found a real conflict in the first wording, and the revision addresses it. But the reader’s written table is explicitly about the requested topics—years, periods, opening and matching—not a clause-by-clause verdict for every category, fixed user sentence, schema description and example. The audit’s own wider read is likewise limited to those topics. That is less than §6 requires, even though the audit calls the blind read a whole-request read. The running second read needs to cover the **whole revised request**, with findings resolved, not just approve the revised sentences. [Blind review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ll-codex.md:13), [audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/PROMPT-AUDIT-c14.md:22), [§6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:192).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lo-codex.md:11:5. **Revised sentences against D433 — consistent with its appended wording note.** The two actual changes match the note: a different year is a separate quantity when each warrants a separate bet, and the closing check specifies the same calendar year for a shared quantity. The revision no longer says that another year cannot be evidence; the existing cross-period evidence instruction remains. I found no additional change in the system, closing or schema files when compared with c8. [D433](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4822), [wording note](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4824), [system](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:102), [cross-period instruction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:67), [closing check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-closing.txt:14).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/is-handoff.md:7:`candidate-closing.txt`, `candidate-schema.json`), and code refuses and sends back once: a reference whose words are not the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/is-handoff.md:11:that D407 dropped (`named`, `main`, `company_states`, `theme_states`), D407 governs: the schema has one `states` field.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/is-handoff.md:16:- the production code they call: `src/hivemind/model.py` (`call`, `build_request`, `check_schema`, `Archive`),\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cs-codex.md:1:**Two issues still block the send.** For example, an article could give a signing date two years away, and the revised schema would permit that date even though the standard caps the check date at 18 months.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cs-codex.md:3:- **Check date:** The schema says to use the date the item supports and applies the 18-month limit only when the item gives none. Apply the limit in both cases.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/u-codex.md:5:- **Keeping every company figure: supported.** In d1-57 draws 1–3, c1 kept the cash-flow figures Alex said to drop. All three accounts cite the unconditional condition instruction. The same wording also appears in the role, closing check and schema, so changing only the condition bullet would leave conflicting instructions.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/u-codex.md:18:- **(b) Agree in principle.** Restore linking to every view informed in **both** places, and check the schema and role for consistency. Test d1-40, d1-57 and d2-66; do not assume this also removes the networking view.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gy-audit-codex.md:7:In the tables, **S** means [system text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt), **J** means [schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json), **P** means [production prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13), and **D** means a decision in the [decision log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:753). Sentence numbers below follow their order within each system-text line. “Consistent” includes format instructions that implement the sourced rule.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hg-codex.md:1:**NOT READY.** The design assumes its schema rejects a six-range answer, but the validator it proposes to use does not enforce the maximum array length. Two engineers could therefore build different behavior, and one could write a ladder with six ranges.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hg-codex.md:3:1. **The five-range limit is not enforced by the specified path.** [DESIGN.md:205](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:205) and [line 473](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:473) rely on the schema for the count. The schema specifies `maxItems: 5` for [ranges](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:169) and states, but [model.check_schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:212) checks only the minimum. The proposed range checks establish a partition, not a count. A six-range theme figure can pass that validator and the stated range checks; the writing rule does not say whether to write six rows or discard one. The reader form assumes five and does not expressly make count a mark, although W could catch it. The fix must specify where the exact count is enforced, cover both arrays, and test a six-item answer through the actual entry point.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hg-codex.md:9:**He’s four findings:** separate archives and cache rejection address the first. The shared exact-decimal rule and boundary examples address the number contract. The refusal and G-accounting rules address the main schema/refusal and G issues, respectively. The archive truncation part remains open, as does malformed-response cost accounting above.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hg-codex.md:11:**What I verified and what remains:** All eight actual fixtures pass the current local schema validator. I did **not** complete the requested independent walk of every fixture’s written rows, every request sentence against its underlying source, the three tables, or every stored reading and score. I therefore cannot certify their consistency, the six lines’ sensitivity, or the absence of another wrong answer that escapes the reader marks. The closing check appears to repeat earlier request rules, and I found no covered-company example in the request; that is not a completed sentence-by-sentence audit.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bp-challenge.md:2:- `why_a_separate_bet`'s description in both schemas now ends \"; for a signing question kept beside an open total of its kind by the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bk-codex.md:9:**SEND WITH CHANGES:** Preserve the separate-judgment and other §4 tests explicitly; make links conditional on relevance and availability; resolve the signed-deal and final-check ordering conflicts; strengthen the controls and falsifiers above; complete the no-cost checks for the changed schema.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hl-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hl-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/a-codex.md:13:   - **Required per-item decision:** require the model to identify an existing relevant question, a justified broader new question, or why neither applies. Source: the standard’s separate evidence and opening judgments. Falsifier: explanations improve but correct filing does not, or small questions increase. The current schema permits empty links without such an account. [Schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/takeover-2026-11-07/k6b-schema.json:134)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bw-challenge.md:1:Whole-request audit of a new arm, c11 (read-only). It is c10a plus one lever: a required `company_impact` field on each new thesis (`arms/c11-schema.json`) and the closing read-back keyed to it (last paragraph of `arms/c11-closing.txt`); `arms/c11-system.txt` equals c10a. Read the whole request as the model reads it (system text with the schema appended, then the payload, then the closing check). Clause by clause, in both directions, against the signed standard (section 3 of the request, D248 boundary 6, D388): is each new sentence consistent, contradicting, wider, narrower or unsourced, and does anything else in the request now contradict it? D248(2), (4) and (5) remain a recorded gap outside this arm. Under 300 words: READY or NOT READY, with each blocking finding.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ln-codex.md:3:I compared all three c14 files with c8: only the sentence in the system text and the parenthetical in the closing check changed; the schema did not.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ln-codex.md:19:- **Company’s own main annual driver — contradicts / keeps narrower.** The standard explicitly permits a question about the annual company figure carrying its value, such as a bank’s net interest income. The request’s four-reason closed set omits that category and says not to open a financial measure’s level, growth, margin or guidance for any period on its own. As written, it excludes a category the standard includes. ([standard, lines 276 and 297](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:276); [c14 system, lines 87–90 and 116–120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-system.txt:87); [c14 schema, lines 49–57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-schema.json:49).)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ln-codex.md:35:- **Period versus settlement date in the schema — ambiguous.** The schema calls `period` “the period or check date that settles the thesis.” For an annual quantity, its covered year and the later release date are distinct; the standard specifies both. The schema can express either as text but does not clearly ask for both, so it risks losing that distinction. Evidence has a separate `evidence_period`, which correctly preserves the period described by the source. ([c14 schema, lines 38–47 and 261–270](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c14-schema.json:38); [standard, lines 276, 279 and 305](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:276).)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jf-challenge.md:5:against\"), `candidate-closing.txt`, `candidate-schema.json` (`reference`), `ladder_step.py` (check 6),\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jf-challenge.md:13:| 4. the midpoint was not D411's; repetition; an event with a reported number and no expectation | the midpoint is gone (row 1); the schema's descriptions are cut to the fields, the paragraph says how to choose, the closing check reads back; \"Otherwise reference is null\" covers the event |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hf-codex.md:11:3. **Malformed or schema-invalid answers lack a Stage A outcome.** [DESIGN.md:344](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:344) defines retries for check refusals, while [model.py:258](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:258) can raise `SchemaError` before those checks. The design must specify first and second failures, archive records, retry, denominator and report; it must also handle the archive’s [200,000-character truncation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:276) when rereading exact numbers.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/eg-codex.md:7:2. **Close Step 1 now, as an accepted component—not as proof the system is ready.** Freeze the adopted c8 request, schema, model settings and retry behavior as the comparison point. Record Ohio as an open defect: c8 missed its separate question in all three development draws. Record the revenue-share opening and unverified passages too. The separate Ohio step remains **unadopted**: its latest trial opened Ohio 9/9 times but also wrongly opened a neighboring case. The fresh acceptance was one draw over a holiday weekend; its results do not establish broad reliability. [D387–D390](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4142), [latest trial](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:2290)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hr-codex.md:11:**Fixture walk.** All eight answers passed the actual production schema validator. The remaining checks are design-level, because the step is not built.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hr-codex.md:30:Walked §5.3, the complete-write tables, all eight answers and projections, the schema, number rule, and the cited validator, storage, date, quote and budget code. **Not reached:** the full request sentence-by-sentence; the individual source and reader-answer rows in `dryrun/`, `dryrun2/packet-a`, `dryrun3/`–`dryrun8/`, and `reference/`; consequently I did not independently verify fixture 6’s source passage or the fixtures’ stated reader results.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gx-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json` and worked examples `examples.json`, as a\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gx-handoff.md:23:3. **The contract (§5, the schema, the examples).** Walk the examples through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ha-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, worked examples `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ha-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ha-handoff.md:34:2. **The contract.** Walk every fixture of `examples.json` through the schema, checks 1 to 8 and the label and number rules. Say\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jx-challenge.md:8:Done, nothing sent: D417 is in the working request and its schema, and in the readers' form's list of allowed refusals.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cu-challenge.md:1:Second revision for your blockers (see \"Second revision\" at the end of `council/cp-claude.md`; files `focused/closing.txt`, `focused/schema.json`, `focused/focused_probe.py`). Under 120 words: SEND / READY, or the blocker.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lv-handoff.md:6:The candidates (in clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/): **c15yc** (system, closing, schema) and **c15c**. Diff each against\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/lv-handoff.md:7:c8-*. Read the whole c15yc request as the model reads it (system text, closing check, schema), against the frozen standard\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hw-audit-codex.md:3:The audit below was written before I opened the author’s mapping or the earlier audits. `S` means the [system text](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt), numbered by line and sentence within that line; `J` means a [schema description](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json); `P` means the [frozen production prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13). “Consistent” includes output formats that implement a sourced rule.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hw-audit-codex.md:69:| J197 `hi` | P35; check 4 | **No investment-standard source for limits:** same as J186. [J197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:197) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hw-audit-codex.md:74:| J263 `due_day_basis` | P16, 26 | **Narrower:** same event-date restriction as S22. [J263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:263) |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hw-audit-codex.md:93:**Number spelling mismatch:** the request and schema constrain value and significant digits, but not token length. Thus `1e+0000`, or `1.0000000000000000000000000000000`, meets the stated numerical limits while [check 4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:348) refuses the spelling. This applies to bounds and reference values. The separate out-of-range-reference and 548-day mismatches found earlier are addressed in the current wording.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ie-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ie-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ie-handoff.md:39:## Your angle: the contract (design §5.3; the field-by-field writes at the head of §5.4; `ladder/examples.json`; `ladder/candidate-schema.json`; `ladder/number_rule_check.py`)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ie-handoff.md:44:1. Walk **each of the eight fixtures** of `examples.json` through the schema (with production's validator, `model.check_schema`\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:30:| `no_ladder` | [19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:19)；D397、D38、v13、16–17 | **更窄**：同 S9。 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:31:| `question` | [44](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:44)；v20–21 | 一致 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:32:| `object` | [49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:49)；v22、`build_prompt` | 一致 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:33:| `not_judged` | [53](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:53)；D397 | **更窄**：同 S6–8。 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:34:| `yes_no`、`yes`、`no` | [74、90、95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:74)；v25 | 一致 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:35:| `states`、`label` | [102、122](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:102)；v25、D38 | 一致；但有上面 S16–18 的覆盖缺口。 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:36:| `figure`、`unit`、`year`、`lo`、`hi` | [134、162、167、190、201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:134)；v26、34–35、`CLOSING` | 一致 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:37:| `favourable_end`、`favourable_why` | [213、217](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:213)；D186、D398 | 一致 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:38:| `reference.words`、`reference.value` | [239、250](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:239)；D260、D398 | 一致 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gw-audit-codex.md:39:| `due_day_basis` | [267](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:267)；v16、26 | 一致 |\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/jy-challenge.md:14:   `by_whom` and `decision`), the typed closing sentence and the typed schema. The stop condition is the first trial's,\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hr-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt`, schema `candidate-schema.json`, check fixtures `examples.json` and the\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hr-handoff.md:10:- **In scope:** the ladder step (§5 to §7 of the design), the request, the schema, the fixtures, and Stage A of the test (§8 up to\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hr-handoff.md:35:## Your angle: the contract (design §5.3; the field-by-field writes at the head of §5.4; `ladder/examples.json`; `ladder/candidate-schema.json`; `ladder/number_rule_check.py`)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/hr-handoff.md:40:1. Walk **each of the eight fixtures** of `examples.json` through the schema (with production's validator, `model.check_schema`\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gn-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt` and schema `candidate-schema.json`, as a design that must be READY before\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gn-handoff.md:18:2. **The contract (§5.1–§5.4, the schema).** Walk these five answers through the schema, checks 1–8 and the label rule, and say what\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/cq-handoff.md:4:`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/focused/` (`system.txt`, `closing.txt`, `schema.json`, `focused_probe.py`, `plan-r16.json`).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gp-codex.md:5:2. **The request and checks still disagree on permitted dates and units.** The request assigns a pending regulatory decision with no date to fiscal year-end ([candidate-system.txt:22](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-system.txt:22)), but defines `period_end` as the end of a period *the topic names*. If it names no period, neither permitted event basis fits. Also, the request asks for a figure’s unit without limiting it, while the [schema’s closed list](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/candidate-schema.json:150) excludes other currencies and units. Specify the accepted response and handling for both cases consistently across request, schema and checks. The year and obligation exceptions, schema reasons, and numeric event-reference conflict raised by go are otherwise corrected.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gp-codex.md:9:4. **Stage A’s comparison is not yet fully buildable or demonstrably fair.** The [control](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:372) has no complete request or answer schema yet, so its ability to return “no ladder,” its retry behaviour and its exposure to the candidate’s extra requirements cannot be audited. Mark F asks for a “bullish end” even on a Yes/No ladder, which has no such labels; define applicability and denominators by shape. Stage A can fail its lines, but specify which marks are applicable before calculating soundness. The maximum is **264 ladders and 528 initial readings**, plus disputes; Stage B estimates **210–360 judgements and 420–720 initial readings**, plus disputes. Packet parallelism is described, but there is still no time or adjudication budget establishing feasibility. Report eligible and unassessable counts per mark and arm.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gp-codex.md:13:6. **Two engineers can implement different year checks.** [DESIGN.md:239](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:239) says figures beyond next year are refused, but the schema accepts any nonblank year. Production’s [`beyond_next_year`](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:577) allows an unparseable string when it contains no four-digit year. Specify the closed accepted year formats, fiscal-year interpretation and refusal behaviour, including invalid and multi-year strings. The old-check table should identify this difference rather than simply saying the check is kept.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gp-codex.md:25:**Request audit.** Line 1 is consistent with the fixed-at-opening design; lines 4–5 with D38/D397; line 6 with the stated exceptions; line 9 with v74i’s object distinction; lines 12–15 with the cited ladder rules, except that requiring *exactly five distinct states* is narrower for an event with three or four possible states. Lines 16–17 follow D260/D398, though applying reference recording to events extends D398’s figure-specific construction. Lines 20–23 follow the cited date rules subject to the date-basis conflict above. The closing check repeats earlier rules; its three sample outcomes cannot prove complete coverage, but it asks the model to check rather than claiming code proves it. The examples do not name the covered company or obviously reproduce a test article. The complete schema and control-request audit remains open.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/x-handoff.md:5:The request as the model reads it: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c2-system.txt` (system), `c2-closing.txt` (appended after the item), `c2-schema.json` (stated in the system text). The control is `clean-arch/takeover-2026-11-07/k6b-*` (diff them).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gh-claude.md:56:   `shared_quantity` (13) or `policy_stage` (8). Stored as themes they bring the theme block, the re-queue rule and the refusal class\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ia-codex.md:22:已逐项读完六条线、计数表、阅读表与请求及 schema 的对应关系，并核对上一轮发现。**未逐条阅读** `dryrun/`、`dryrun2/packet-a`、`dryrun3/`–`dryrun8/` 和 `reference/` 的各个存档答案及计数脚本；这些存档数量由另一角度复核。\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gk-challenge.md:65:- **Answer, strict schema:** `settles`; `not_judged` (each other part, with why); `object` (the ticker or a listed theme id);\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/ae-codex.md:15:- **Cut-answer retry and changed test — revise.** Alex authorized one retry for non-JSON or schema failures, and stopping for other failures. The code treats every `finish_reason=length` as a format failure *before parsing*; an existing test supplies syntactically valid JSON with that finish reason. A cut response can be incomplete even when JSON parses, but the claim that every cut answer “is not JSON” is false. Clarify that boundary against Alex’s decision rather than treating the old test as proven wrong. [Decision]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/takeover-2026-11-07/LOG.md:763), [code]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/runner.py:300), [test]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/test_runner.py:366).\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-A.md:20:- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-A.md:124:- fresh-9/T1 [shared_quantity]: Will the combined capital expenditures of the top five hyperscalers approach $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027, after about $800 billion in 2026, as Nvidia expects? (period: Calendar 2027 (with 2026 as the base year); checkable from the hyperscalers' full-year 2027 capex disclosures in their fourth-quarter reports in early 2028.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-A.md:125:- fresh-9/T2 [shared_quantity]: Will the combined capital expenditures of the top five hyperscalers approach $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027, as Nvidia expects? (period: Calendar 2027; settled after the top five hyperscalers report Q4 2027 results in early 2028.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-A.md:127:- fresh-9/T4 [shared_quantity]: Will the top five hyperscalers' combined capital expenditures approach $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027, as Nvidia expects? (period: Calendar 2027; the aggregate becomes checkable after the five companies report fourth-quarter 2027 results (early 2028), the release date of the full-year figure.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-A.md:129:- fresh-9/T6 [shared_quantity]: Will the combined capital expenditures of the top five hyperscalers approach the $1.3 trillion Nvidia expects for calendar 2027? (period: Calendar 2027 (next calendar year relative to the September 2026 item), checked against the hyperscalers' quarterly capex in 10-Q/10-K filings and tallied at their full-year 2027 reports in early 2028.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-A.md:204:- fresh-24/T2 [shared_quantity]: Will the Federal Reserve raise its policy rate by a quarter point at its September 15-16, 2026 meeting? (period: The September 15-16, 2026 FOMC meeting; the decision is announced at the close of the meeting on September 16, 2026, so the answer is known that day.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/bq-packet-A.md:205:- fresh-24/T3 [shared_quantity]: Will the Federal Reserve raise its policy rate at the September 15-16, 2026 FOMC meeting, as markets price roughly a 60% probability — a decision the item says could directly affect financing costs for the AI data-center buildout? (period: September 15-16, 2026 FOMC meeting; set by the meeting date the item states.)\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gq-codex.md:3:1. **A missing reference passes unnoticed by code.** [DESIGN.md:245](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:245) checks a reference *if supplied*; the schema permits `reference: null`. A company revenue ladder can have five valid ranges and `reference: null` even when the article states guidance. It passes checks 1–8, but §5.3 does not list **omitting an existing reference** among their limits. Stage A’s X also does not clearly fail this case: it requires the candidate’s field to quote an expectation where one exists, but the “sound” comparison includes that candidate-only clause. Add the missing-reference example and its reader verdict; separate the common comparison from the candidate-only contract.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gq-codex.md:5:2. **The control is treated differently in ways that can change the result.** [DESIGN.md:378](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:378) gives the control a mandatory `year` for **every** ladder, including events ([control schema:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/control-schema.json:29)); the candidate has code derive an event’s year. The control also receives a vague instruction to return `no_ladder` when rules disallow one, without the candidate’s explicit four cases. Further, X includes a candidate-only field but is included in both arms’ “sound” totals ([DESIGN.md:401](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:401)). Specify common eligibility and common marks separately from candidate-only requirements, including event-year handling and refusal rules. The comparison can fail, but its present result would not isolate the designs fairly.\nclean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/gq-codex.md:9:4. **The accepted contract is still ambiguous.** [DESIGN.md:234](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:234) permits `other` units but says they render as bare numbers; [line 269](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:269) says another unit cannot be expressed. The request requires that unit in the question. State whether the unit is accepted, exactly what the judge sees, and how it is checked. Also, check 5 searches `looks_at` and question, but `looks_at` is only later defined as `outcome` ([line 284](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md:284)); name that input at the check. The schema permits a bare calendar year for a company figure even though the request requires its fiscal year; say whether a mismatch is refused or only judged by Y.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
